{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming","id":1335938,"title":"Consent in Gaming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-15T12:55:37-07:00","id":1335938,"title":"Consent in Gaming","content":"In new free e-book - <a href=\"https://www.montecookgames.com/consent-in-gaming/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Consent in Gaming</b></a> - <i>Monte Cook Games</i> is pointing on discussing sensitive and mature topics on RPG sessions. I'm opening this forum topic for discussion on this subjects.<br /> <br /> One of example tools showed in <b>CiG </b>is <i>Consent Checklist</i> ( see below ). <b>What do you think about it?</b> What are your tricks for make players more comfortable at the table?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://scontent.frix7-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/70319930_10212682165323920_9104131723104354304_n.jpg?_nc_cat=104&amp;_nc_eui2=AeEWcMqcW6-vLN8666dKLjhjdY4cYZWSF4wguA4r1NMRgnOTvDZCskOJurU50T5JeC4OWP1rlFBj3dI4gmvhD31kbefMewuzr1j_w6i10EbKbw&amp;_nc_oc=AQkfNBE9jmqc-hqX0J6-mNzNQ2wF-CawdGu4JoG2Xk60yZ_ipH-GeExaxeOtw1qeTjI&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.frix7-1.fna&amp;oh=ed3bc835b4ebf383d398af587dda7d04&amp;oe=5DF3EEC0\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-18-2019, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T14:09:49-07:00","id":1335942,"title":"","content":"I've seen this form pop up on some other gaming forums and get talked about, some a-holes chimed in and called people names if you can't handling this stuff, not hard to imagine that someone is gonna say such things<br /> <br /> But for me: Can be a good idea for sure, seems like things could/should be talked about as a group<br /> <br /> Dunno if that would have prevented one recent thing, but a DM posted a thing in a PBP game and I started having a panic attack, I took it to be that my goblin wizard was getting child molested, I lost a lot of sleep but didn't say anything of the things I was feeling, but my fighting back finally got the DM to end it in a huff<br /> <br /> I couldn't even really deal with it for a few weeks, finally was able to examine things and then talk to the DM, he apologized right away and I could sleep all night again, and here I am 52 years old. I wouldn't say I'm the biggest snowflake ever, but it still affected me greatly<br /> <br /> Honestly, I like a little romance, and like having my characters in relationships a lot of the time. I recently started playing a Gnoll cleric, and wasn't even expecting her to get in a relationship, but I was feeling real good when a Minotaur fighter in the group had an instant crush on her, still early, but it's fun already<br /> <br /> As much as I love some romance, fade to black is good for me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24473,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","user":"Willowfang","date":". 09-15-2019, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T14:41:59-07:00","id":1335948,"title":"","content":"First, it's better that we're talking about active discussions of these things even if people don't like the tools. Far too often people left too much of this unspoken and don't realize it.<br /> <br /> The form's a decent approach for some styles of games. I would use it for conventions (where there's time to send it out to people that reserve seats ahead of time), new gamers in the group, or for larger groups like LARPs or chat games where it's just hard to keep so many people on the same page. Like all of these tools, it's not perfect or right for every situation, but it has its place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T13:11:28-07:00","id":1336083,"title":"","content":"Discussion about safety tools in gaming are a great way to filter out people you absolutely never want to share a table with. I can't begin to grasp why the subject brings out the biggest, proudest assholes in the entire hobby, but boy howdy does it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T15:25:02-07:00","id":1336105,"title":"","content":"My default assumption to most &quot;mature&quot; games is that it's running somewhere in the R rating category. And while I personally like to take the &quot;anything goes&quot; approach in regards to content, I am too self conscious about sitting around the table and publicly engaging in ERP with people while everybody else watches. Unless it's a group orgy scene, we're cutting to black when moments like that happen! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the topic of racism, religion and cultural issues, I'd green light that in the case of fantasy context. Nobody is actually getting triggered when the light skinned High Elves and dark skinned Drow try to kill each other on sight. And I prefer my Orcs and Goblinoids to be slave trading, rape crazed barbarians. But if a player decides to start spewing obscenities at real world cultures and ethnic groups, then I'd start making sure I was out of punching distance, before things escalated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T16:00:10-07:00","id":1336110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336105#post1336105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the topic of racism, religion and cultural issues, I'd green light that in the case of fantasy context. Nobody is actually getting triggered when the light skinned High Elves and dark skinned Drow try to kill each other on sight. And I prefer my Orcs and Goblinoids to be slave trading, rape crazed barbarians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I pretty much want to never be anywhere near your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T16:38:03-07:00","id":1336117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336110#post1336110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I pretty much want to never be anywhere near your table.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Once again, &quot;in the case of fantasy context.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also once again, <i>&quot;we're cutting to black when moments like that happen!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-16-2019, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T17:52:39-07:00","id":1336128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336105#post1336105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the topic of racism, ***SNIP*** Nobody is actually getting triggered when ***SNIP***</div> </div> </div> </div>So a lot of snipping there, and just in regards to what's left...<br /> <br /> There is a game where the high elf wizard is an elf supremacist and was treating my 18 year female old human rogue like shit all the time. A rare conflux to be sure, and more a matter of him treating me like shit than the racism, but constantly harassing another player is not cool. So you may need to disallow something if it affects a player within the party<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T18:15:22-07:00","id":1336130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Willowfang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336128#post1336128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So a lot of snipping there, and just in regards to what's left...<br /> <br /> There is a game where the high elf wizard is an elf supremacist and was treating my 18 year female old human rogue like shit all the time. A rare conflux to be sure, and more a matter of him treating me like shit than the racism, but constantly harassing another player is not cool. So you may need to disallow something if it affects a player within the party</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At no point did I advocate directing such behavior towards your fellow players. If that kind of stuff is going on, then yeah, you've got a problem that should be addressed as soon as possible.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to in game characters, though? Sure, go for it!<br /> <br /> Also &quot;high elf supremacist...&quot; so basically a high elf? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-16-2019, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T18:19:58-07:00","id":1336132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336117#post1336117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, &quot;in the case of fantasy context.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a meaningless context. Someone wrote a fantasy RPG that was white/Christian supremacist garbage where Jews are goblins and Muslims are orcs. Dressing it up in the cloak of fantasy didn't make it any less offensive. Rape is rape. My opinions on how it should be handled in an RPG has nothing to do with genre. A whole race of sapient and sentient beings that are slavers and rapists isn't really something that's lacking in issues to include just because you FtB.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T20:09:19-07:00","id":1336140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336132#post1336132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a meaningless context. Someone wrote a fantasy RPG that was white/Christian supremacist garbage where Jews are goblins and Muslims are orcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they friggin aren't. In my setting, Goblins are Goblins and Orcs are Orcs.<br /> <br /> Tolkien can kiss my ass!<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> and honestly, it's exactly because the races are portrayed as savage monsters that makes them so appealing to me. The idea that there are races in the setting which spit in the face of civilized society, giving in to their savage impulses, their twisted desires, and worshiping deities which support and encourage this kind of behavior. That is what makes them so fascinating to me. When you try to take such creatures and make them more nuanced, then you take away the very thing that makes them special. At that point, they're nothing more than one of the core races wearing a different skin; and thus I see no reason to even play them anymore.<br /> <br /> Or explore their society for that matter. What are nuanced Orcs? Slightly dumber Half Orcs. What are nuanced Goblins? An uglier version of Halflings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-17-2019, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T20:17:41-07:00","id":1336143,"title":"","content":"Sorry I didn't some how make it clear or think to do so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> I didn't think or mean to implay you were advocating anything of the sort, just the word you used touched on something I'm going through<br /> <br /> this elf was being very Elves are the best and humans are beneath us and being very abusive about it to my human character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T20:29:46-07:00","id":1336144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Willowfang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336143#post1336143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry I didn't some how make it clear or think to do so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> I didn't think or mean to implay you were advocating anything of the sort, just the word you used touched on something I'm going through<br /> <br /> this elf was being very Elves are the best and humans are beneath us and being very abusive about it to my human character</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, sorry to hear that. Hopefully it remains only in character, and doesn't spill out into something relating to real life.<br /> <br /> Though to be honest, I've kind of got my own High Elf Wizard who would behave in a similar fashion. The guy just really, really hates human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T22:51:47-07:00","id":1336154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336140#post1336140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they friggin aren't. In my setting, Goblins are Goblins and Orcs are Orcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>But these are two keep problems.<br /> <br /> First is, &quot;in my setting.&quot; That's why &quot;fantasy context&quot; is meaningless. Your fantasy setting might not have purposefully coded things that way, someone else's fantasy setting did. They're both equally fantasy settings even if of wildly different quality. I mean, Tolkien explicitly wanted his dwarvess to be read as Jews, even if he felt it was a positive thing since they're generally on the good side and all (not that it necessarily feels that way to Jews).<br /> <br /> Fantasy context just means, &quot;whatever context the author wants to be, painted with genre stuff,&quot; hence the way you used it doesn't mean anything.<br /> <br /> &quot;Goblins are Goblins and Orcs are Orcs,&quot; is another problem. They're not real things. I can't go somewhere on Earth, find a real goblin, and say, &quot;OK, this is what a goblin is.&quot; They're made up. There's hundreds if not thousands of interpretations of what Goblins or Orcs are. Trying to claim there's some sort of Platonic ideal of them just doesn't work. And the interpretation of them that you use is going to matter to people (whether it will turn them off, or appeal to them, as tastes dictate).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and honestly, it's exactly because the races are portrayed as savage monsters that makes them so appealing to me. </div> </div> </div>If you want savage monsters, just have savage monsters. &quot;Race&quot; is a loaded term you don't need to have savage monsters.<br /> <br /> We don't need demons to be a &quot;race&quot; they can just be demons and evil and bad.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T23:27:59-07:00","id":1336155,"title":"","content":"So, on the subject of fantasy racism, I\u2019d like to approach the subject from a slightly different angle. You know how, in Scarred Lands, the whole barefoot halfling thing is actually a stereotype derived from the caricature of halfling slaves? That\u2019s a way to address themes of racism in an RPG that I personally love. It acknowledges the common fantasy trope, gives it an in-fiction explanation, and encourages players to think beyond the trope, and indeed to recontextualize the trope as unfairly limiting to the race\u2019s potential characterization. Furthermore, it provides an analogue to the ways oppressive ideas become ingrained in cultural consciousness and can be oppressive even without conscious mal-intent. And it does so as a background worldbuilding element, rather than forcing players into potentially uncomfortable situations where their character is being actively oppressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T04:23:57-07:00","id":1336179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336154#post1336154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Goblins are Goblins and Orcs are Orcs,&quot; is another problem. They're not real things. I can't go somewhere on Earth, find a real goblin, and say, &quot;OK, this is what a goblin is.&quot; They're made up. There's hundreds if not thousands of interpretations of what Goblins or Orcs are. Trying to claim there's some sort of Platonic ideal of them just doesn't work. And the interpretation of them that you use is going to matter to people (whether it will turn them off, or appeal to them, as tastes dictate).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I understand that. What I meant to say wasn't intended to be <i>&quot;I am portraying a mythologically accurate version of Orcs and Goblins&quot;</i> but was supposed to be <i>&quot;this is not an allegory for any real world culture, stop accusing me of being racist.&quot;</i> Not that I'm saying anybody here was, but there are obviously those out there who would try to superimpose various ideologies unto the setting and mistake it for some kind of personal attack.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I thought they were barefoot, because the soles of their feet were as tough as leather. So trying to wear shoes would be unnecessary for protecting their feet, beyond hygiene reasons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-17-2019, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T06:09:35-07:00","id":1336191,"title":"","content":"People may want to chill on uncharitably reading Nyrufa's posts.<br /> <br /> It may be good to have for Conventions, but for playing with friends I prefer an oral contract rather than a full blown written one. So just talk with the players to get a sense of what buttons to hold off on pressing.<br /> <br /> I mean honestly the only time I use the term race is with RPGs and it feels archaic even there. Species and civilization would work better in my opinion.<br /> <br /> But it has Rats and Spiders as triggering. I can see vomiting as I've known people who can't even hear about vomiting without panicking but if you are triggered by rats and spiders to an extent where that would be a deal breaker you should probably talk to your game master, it feels rather unnecessary to have on a list like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T07:56:46-07:00","id":1336212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336179#post1336179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I thought they were barefoot, because the soles of their feet were as tough as leather. So trying to wear shoes would be unnecessary for protecting their feet, beyond hygiene reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's general Halflings. Halflings were D&amp;D's &quot;Hobbit race&quot; and like Hobbits, they tended to have very hairy feet with thick soles. As a result, they preferred not to wear shoes since, not because of anything racist, but simply because of how hairy their feet were, they found stuffing their feet into shoes uncomfortable, and due to the thick soles of their feet, shoes largely unnecessary. Some, of course, liked to wear shoes for various reasons, but those reasons tended to be fairly personal.<br /> <br /> But the Scarred Lands has its own take on Halflings, and I'd guess their feet aren't as hairy and the soles of their feet aren't as thick, so unlike say, Forgotten Realms halflings, these guys Halflings probably wear shoes, in spite of various racist rumors about why they typically don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T09:00:18-07:00","id":1336221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336212#post1336212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's general Halflings. Halflings were D&amp;D's &amp;quot;Hobbit race&amp;quot; and like Hobbits, they tended to have very hairy feet with thick soles. As a result, they preferred not to wear shoes since, not because of anything racist, but simply because of how hairy their feet were, they found stuffing their feet into shoes uncomfortable, and due to the thick soles of their feet, shoes largely unnecessary. Some, of course, liked to wear shoes for various reasons, but those reasons tended to be fairly personal.<br /> <br /> But the Scarred Lands has its own take on Halflings, and I'd guess their feet aren't as hairy and the soles of their feet aren't as thick, so unlike say, Forgotten Realms halflings, these guys Halflings probably wear shoes, in spite of various racist rumors about why they typically don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. The soles of one\u2019s feet tend to get pretty calloused and thick when one\u2019s masters don\u2019t provide them with shoes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T10:31:02-07:00","id":1336239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336191#post1336191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People may want to chill on uncharitably reading Nyrufa's posts.<br /> <br /> It may be good to have for Conventions, but for playing with friends I prefer an oral contract rather than a full blown written one. So just talk with the players to get a sense of what buttons to hold off on pressing.<br /> <br /> I mean honestly the only time I use the term race is with RPGs and it feels archaic even there. Species and civilization would work better in my opinion.<br /> <br /> But it has Rats and Spiders as triggering. I can see vomiting as I've known people who can't even hear about vomiting without panicking but if you are triggered by rats and spiders to an extent where that would be a deal breaker you should probably talk to your game master, it feels rather unnecessary to have on a list like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, then you personally wouldn't use the one in the Monte Cook book. Maybe your oral agreement is your own, maybe you base it off the given one in the book. If that works for your group, and folks can let you know in some way what might be too much for them, then that is pretty much the whole point of their book.<br /> <br /> Rats and Spiders are just some of the included examples. I've already seen a poster on the RPGnet thread about this talk about how his wife can get through hearing the word spider OK, but when the spider miniatures came out, she had to leave. So, already, there is somebody out there that would be checking off the Spiders example. Maybe nobody in <i>your </i>group checks those boxes as bad - good to know isn't it? - but then they add in on a blank line &quot;Elephants&quot;. Now you know that adding elephants to your adventure might cause difficulties for them, and you can act accordingly.<br /> <br /> That's how the tool provided can be used. Doesn't work for you and your group, that doesn't mean it has no use with other groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T12:04:32-07:00","id":1336268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336179#post1336179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but was supposed to be <i>&quot;this is not an allegory for any real world culture, stop accusing me of being racist.&quot;</i> Not that I'm saying anybody here was, but there are obviously those out there who would try to superimpose various ideologies unto the setting and mistake it for some kind of personal attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is just a cop out.<br /> <br /> The second you say something like, &quot;goblins are an evil race,&quot; you've made them an allegory for real world cultural issues. Maybe you avoid racism, or classism, or whatever, but &quot;race&quot; is a fictional concept humans made up as an excuse to be shitty to each other. When you call something in your fantasy world a &quot;race&quot; you're saying, &quot;you should consider these analogues to humans,&quot; and then people are going to be primed to look at the context you put in your setting. You can't just say, &quot;Goblins are goblins, and they're a race,&quot; and then say, &quot;don't read anything into this.&quot; Calling them a race is asking them to read into it. And either you acknowledge that and make sure your message is clear, or you don't.<br /> <br /> Just blaming people that are trying to &quot;superimpose&quot; is abdicating your responsibilities in crafting your setting. If you write a setting, you're responsible for what you put in it. If you put in stuff that's reads as extremely _____-ist, that's your fault, not some fictional group of people out to get offended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336212#post1336212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a result, they preferred not to wear shoes since, not because of anything racist, but simply because of how hairy their feet were, they found stuffing their feet into shoes uncomfortable, and due to the thick soles of their feet, shoes largely unnecessary. Some, of course, liked to wear shoes for various reasons, but those reasons tended to be fairly personal.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not in the novels themselves, Tolkien actually wrote notes on the subject. He never intended the Hobbits to be read as &quot;anti-shoes,&quot; but rather that the Shire was such a nice place shoes were irrelevant for them given the terrain of their homeland. Hobbits that travel outside the Shire almost always end up wearing shoes when doing so, because the rest of the world isn't all soft grassy hills and farmland.<br /> <br /> But since hobbits are isolationists by culture, Hobbits wearing shoes in the Shire are basically being anti-social because they're signalling that they don't consider the Shire &quot;home&quot; by wearing something that's for &quot;outside.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, with Tolkien, it's generally better to look at classism before racism for the underlying assumptions being made. The hobbits were Tolkien's idealized bucolic agrarian class, having their folksy charm, generous hospitality, and balanced lifestyles being destroyed by industrialization to turn them into middle class factory workers. They were written as not wearing shoes for the same reason Huck Finn doesn't wear shoes: it's a metaphor for the freedom from higher class social constraints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T12:49:16-07:00","id":1336287,"title":"","content":"Dang I misclicked on my phone and lost my post. I\u2019ll type it out when I get home but I\u2019ll respond to this one though since it\u2019s a simple response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336221#post1336221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. The soles of one\u2019s feet tend to get pretty calloused and thick when one\u2019s masters don\u2019t provide them with shoes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they fall off or you die from necrosis when you walk in the icy mountains like the furry footed burrowers do in Middle Earth with no issue. It sounds like shoe wearing Halflings are clearly morphologically different from the assumed default core Halfling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T13:12:44-07:00","id":1336292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336268#post1336268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But this is just a cop out.<br /> <br /> The second you say something like, &quot;goblins are an evil race,&quot; you've made them an allegory for real world cultural issues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I vehemently refuse to believe this, and there is nothing anybody can say on this or any other forum to convince me otherwise. I use the word &quot;race&quot; as synonymous with &quot;sapient species.&quot; So when it comes from me, I am not saying that the particular culture should be compared to those of humans. I'm merely acknowledging the fact that the species has gained self awareness, and the ability to formulate its own society. If aliens suddenly landed on planet earth, would you argue our civilization using the word &quot;race&quot; when referring to their people?<br /> <br /> When I apply the description of &quot;evil&quot; to a race, I do so in a fashion similar to those of Fiends, Celestials and other outsiders. Their evil behavior is deeply ingrained into them on an instinctual level, rather than it being a conscious act of will. Of course, being self aware, they have the capacity to fight against those instincts if they feel so inclined. But it is always going to be an uphill battle, since following the evil path comes natural to them.<br /> <br /> And when it comes to a fantasy setting, I can make this into an objective fact, backed up by mountains of imperial evidence. Yes, I am fully aware that this is not how things work in real life. Which is why it's a good thing that RPG's aren't real life, and therefor are not beholden to its rules.<br /> <br /> To borrow a quote from South Park, of all things <i>&quot;God damn it, there are no themes! Stop reading into stuff that isn't there!&quot;</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-17-2019, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T13:50:56-07:00","id":1336299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336292#post1336292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If aliens suddenly landed on planet earth, would you argue our civilization using the word &quot;race&quot; when referring to their people?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, <i>I</i> would dispute it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T14:29:53-07:00","id":1336311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336268#post1336268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But this is just a cop out.<br /> <br /> The second you say something like, &amp;quot;goblins are an evil race,&amp;quot; you've made them an allegory for real world cultural issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Who says that? <br /> <br /> You?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T14:42:50-07:00","id":1336316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336292#post1336292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vehemently refuse to believe this, and there is nothing anybody can say on this or any other forum to convince me otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a very useful thing to say.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's a very useful thing to say if you want to protect people that want to use RPGs to be assholes to other people. Otherwise it's not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I use the word &quot;race&quot; as synonymous with &quot;sapient species.&quot; </div> </div> </div>You shouldn't. It's a bad habit that directly stems from racist ideology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So when it comes from me, I am not saying that the particular culture should be compared to those of humans. </div> </div> </div>So, like I said. It's a cop out. You're abdicating your responsibility as an author to choose your words carefully to communicate your intended meaning to other people, and then getting defensive when they know what the word means to everyone else, rather than just what you've decided it should mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If aliens suddenly landed on planet earth, would you argue our civilization using the word &quot;race&quot; when referring to their people? </div> </div> </div>I would vociferously object as both someone that cares about not being dumb with words - esp. in a first contact situation - and as a biologist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I apply the description of &quot;evil&quot; to a race, I do so in a fashion similar to those of Fiends, Celestials and other outsiders. Their evil behavior is deeply ingrained into them on an instinctual level, rather than it being a conscious act of will. Of course, being self aware, they have the capacity to fight against those instincts if they feel so inclined. But it is always going to be an uphill battle, since following the evil path comes natural to them. </div> </div> </div>But you yourself said you want Orcs and Goblins that aren't nuanced or complex...this is nuance. If they are self-aware to know that they've being evil, and could choose to not be evil, then their evil is a moral failing no matter what their instincts, and they're not just savage monsters to have a power fantasy by killing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And when it comes to a fantasy setting, I can make this into an objective fact, backed up by mountains of imperial evidence. </div> </div> </div>And that choice is a conscious act on your part, which is something everyone that has any interaction with your setting is within their rights to critique. Any stupid things you decide to encode into your setting is stuff people have every right to call out for being stupid, and more so because you yourself are the only person to blame for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is why it's a good thing that RPG's aren't real life, and therefor are not beholden to its rules. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the people that play it are, even you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To borrow a quote from South Park, of all things <i>&quot;God damn it, there are no themes! Stop reading into stuff that isn't there!&quot;</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>This whole attitude is one of the reasons why we have things like this consent form in the first place. The general RPG world wants to claim their more than adult enough to not need these tools, but then want to wave incredibly immature thinking in other people's faces.<br /> <br /> We need consent tools because you sound - whether you intend to or not, or care or not - like the kind of person that would subject their players without warning or consent, to the graphic depictions of children being raped and then cannibalized, and then when everyone gets upset, you'd insist everyone but you is the problem.<br /> <br /> Someone that seriously says, &quot;there are no themes, stop reading into stuff,&quot; is someone who's only goal is to cause others emotional harm; and I absolutely believe that's true about the South Park creators. Because they said so. They just claim causing harm to as many people as possible somehow makes it OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T14:50:01-07:00","id":1336321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336311#post1336311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Who says that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone that's spent at last 30 minutes seriously studying the concept of race as a way to classify different groups of humans should be saying that, and if they're not... I'd be very worried about the conclusions they've drawn about why racism is a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T14:58:52-07:00","id":1336325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336321#post1336321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone that's spent at last 30 minutes seriously studying the concept of race as a way to classify different groups of humans should be saying that, and if they're not... I'd be very worried about the conclusions they've drawn about why racism is a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's easy. Justice. No one controls who they're born as. Including race. So treating and mistreating people over something they have no control over is wrong.<br /> <br /> So let's say I snap my fingers. Antlike race. Like the zerg or tyranids. Highly adaptive and able to transform themselves to meet any task. Computers are actually breeds with increased brain density and atrophied bodies, cleaning and repairing machines are droned with automated responses and a spider-like body plan. They don't view other species as people and they serve as a bad guy, slicing and shooting up innocent people out of sheer apathy. Their ships are gigeresque horrors.<br /> <br /> I did this without any thought of race. No relation of skin colour or geography. No thought given to racial history. <br /> <br /> Now, how racist is this example? What allegory can you make from it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:07:02-07:00","id":1336330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336239#post1336239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, then you personally wouldn't use the one in the Monte Cook book. Maybe your oral agreement is your own, maybe you base it off the given one in the book. If that works for your group, and folks can let you know in some way what might be too much for them, then that is pretty much the whole point of their book.<br /> <br /> Rats and Spiders are just some of the included examples. I've already seen a poster on the RPGnet thread about this talk about how his wife can get through hearing the word spider OK, but when the spider miniatures came out, she had to leave. So, already, there is somebody out there that would be checking off the Spiders example. Maybe nobody in <i>your </i>group checks those boxes as bad - good to know isn't it? - but then they add in on a blank line &quot;Elephants&quot;. Now you know that adding elephants to your adventure might cause difficulties for them, and you can act accordingly.<br /> <br /> That's how the tool provided can be used. Doesn't work for you and your group, that doesn't mean it has no use with other groups.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay I am reading some hostility in this response, and maybe I'm wrong because this is typing and tone doesn't always have 100% Clarity. I never said this is something people shouldn't do or its wrong, I said I would prefer not to do this because I only play table top games with my personal friends. Contracts are made to protect certain parties in an agreement, ideally all parties but these type of things are made bare minimum to cover the GM's ass. It rather than just watch out for my own bum I want my players to know they can talk with me about issues with the game or even change or clarify things, rather than have that extra step of a physical contract.<br /> <br /> Writing game notes is for characters and setting and not for the players. Having a physical contract you have everyone sign to play a game comes off as cold and sterile. I prefer to talk with my players and develop a rapport. When you just have someone check mark and sign a preprinted document there is a lot of room for people overlook things, and I know a lot people who find even one page character sheets too much information. Personally I like to have at least those two page sheets if not the four page ones. But you should talk with your players and find out what is okay, and what are some expectations for the game. If you have people fill out a form it does not have the same personal touch and things can be overlooked or unclear. I even said it could be a useful tool for con games.<br /> <br /> But for some people, I would argue a lot of people, they would find it uncomfortable to put on paper a list of deepest soul deep fears, especially when you can just talk privately to your game master. Its not really fun to have someone be able to look at a glance and know vulnerable aspects of who you are, concerning things like assault and other traumatic experiences, and I don't think people should have to fill out such a form if they don't want to, as a game master you are not entitled to such intimate knowledge when they can just have a private discussion away from the group.<br /> <br /> I pointed out I had an issue with the arbitrary inclusion of Spiders and Rats because that should be represented by the fill in the blank option, otherwise why don't you have Centipedes and Snakes? Centipedes and Snakes are just as likely to be a fear as Spiders and Rats, and I would argue more people are afraid of Centipedes then they are of Spiders. Everyone I know who is afraid of spiders also fears centipedes, meanwhile I know people who won't bat an eye at a spider but do not want to have anything to do with centipedes. What about Dogs? I love dogs personally, but people who are afraid of dogs usually have it rooted in a traumatic childhood memory. My point is it is arbitrary to just have Spiders and Rats on the sheet, its not so common that it needs to be on there because if it needs to be on there then other things need to be on there as well. I never said there was nobody who can't deal with Arachnid imagery, I'm saying that is what the fill in the blank space is for.<br /> <br /> Just talk with your players, its common sense if you are playing with a friend and she lost her eye to a dog mauling that you shouldn't rub that in their face. Lists aren't comprehensive so it is better to have them just tell you rather than play 20 Questions. This has been in the books for a long time, books from your company, they say talk to your players. This sheet can be a useful tool but it doesn't replace actually communication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:19:18-07:00","id":1336333,"title":"","content":"It's specifically on a list so you don't need to get into the details of why you are afraid of spiders and not centipedes, or centipedes and not spiders, so you don't have to justify triggers to people you don't know and can just trust that they won't use them against you.<br /> <br /> I appreciate a lot of us play with people we have played with for years and know very well, but there's always new people coming into the community and even the people we do know can change, and with the surge of online gaming there's a lot of people getting into games without knowing much about the others they're playing with. So a Nyrufa-equivalent doesn't have to, after they've gathered their players, say 'Oh by the way, I run games with slavery and rape,' and now players might want to bail because to him it was a default assumption and to others it's a traumatic event. Sure, if you know you're playing with a friend who lost her eye to a dog mauling it can be a sensitive issue. But not everyone knows the personal history of everyone they game with and Anon4 doesn't have to stop the game after you introduce an eye-eating dog and explain why they have an issue with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:24:14-07:00","id":1336334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336316#post1336316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Too Heated Personal Attacks</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude come on you don't need to make personal attacks. You disagree with him, you don't need to call him his opinions stupid. It's not helpful. It's rude. It will only escalate meaningless arguments and makes it just seem you are just talking at somebody. And when you just talk at somebody rather than talk with somebody it comes off as having some sort of baggage or projection regardless if that is true or not.<br /> <br /> Very few people believe Dwarves are allegories to Hebrews in Lord of the Rings, even if it's true. Not everything is an allegory, otherwise, everything is an allegory and that isn't helpful...<br /> <br /> Look Race is an outdated term and I don't think its useful to be included in RPGs, yet they have it already coded into the grammar. This is why when I ask a question on the D&amp;D 5th ed Facebook group about &quot;what happens when a Half-Elf or Half-Orc has child, is it another Half-Elf/Half-Orc or is it the parent's race?&quot; the mods remove the question and state you can't ask those questions because people give icky answers. Well they should have thought about that before describing the name of a Splat as your Race.<br /> <br /> In games you can have species or civilization, you don't need race. In the real world you have ethnicity and nationality I should have to label a &quot;race&quot; on every damn form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:28:21-07:00","id":1336338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336292#post1336292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vehemently refuse to believe this, and there is nothing anybody can say on this or any other forum to convince me otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are easier ways to say &quot;I'm not going to discuss this in good faith.&quot; There are easier ways to say &quot;I'm okay with being part of the problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> We've been round this conversation circle a whole damn lot with you, and I think it's clear you're comfortable with your positions, which includes a lot of other people strongly objecting to yours. Sooooo what are you trying to do here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-17-2019, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:29:55-07:00","id":1336339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336325#post1336325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's easy. Justice. No one controls who they're born as. Including race. So treating and mistreating people over something they have no control over is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just describing what's wrong with discrimination, not what's specifically wrong with racism.<br /> <br /> To ask a probing question regarding your phrasing: Is holding racists beliefs bad even if you never actively do something racist? If someone thinks black people are bad, but never meets a black person to mistreat... is that neutral, or wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did this without any thought of race. No relation of skin colour or geography. No thought given to racial history. </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's a fairly weak example that didn't really pay much attention to what it's trying to contradict so... maybe some more thought was needed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, how racist is this example? What allegory can you make from it? </div> </div> </div>First, lets go back a bit:<br /> <br /> The second you say something like, &quot;goblins are an evil race,&quot; you've made them an allegory for real world cultural issues. Maybe you avoid racism, or classism, or whatever, but &quot;race&quot; is a fictional concept humans made up as an excuse to be shitty to each other. When you call something in your fantasy world a &quot;race&quot; you're saying, &quot;you should consider these analogues to humans,&quot; and then people are going to be primed to look at the context you put in your setting.<br /> <br /> This is what I said in full, rather than just trying to snip it a bit. So &quot;how racist is this example,&quot; isn't a valid question.<br /> <br /> As for allegories?<br /> <br /> Insect-like species, especially eusocial ones with high levels of morphological specialization, are most frequently used with highly Marxist connotations, especially of the Red Scare type. Ant-like humans... like a single party system ruled by a despot, where workers and soldiers are treated as interchangeable drones and service to the state is all they live for. Soviet architecture is referred to as brutal (like those grotesque ships of yours). The populace accepted vicious purges both internally and externally of those that went against the state. The Zerg Rush is directly analogous to Soviet WWII combat tactics knowing that they had superior numbers compared to the Germans and would win a war of attrition by using simple designs that were easy to train people on.<br /> <br /> Of course, is less WH40K or Starship Troopers, where the default situation isn't war, you'll see a more of a European style liberal socialist allegory to contrast against the American capitalist humans or what not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:38:43-07:00","id":1336343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336333#post1336333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's specifically on a list so you don't need to get into the details of why you are afraid of spiders and not centipedes, or centipedes and not spiders, so you don't have to justify triggers to people you don't know and can just trust that they won't use them against you.<br /> <br /> I appreciate a lot of us play with people we have played with for years and know very well, but there's always new people coming into the community and even the people we do know can change, and with the surge of online gaming there's a lot of people getting into games without knowing much about the others they're playing with. So a Nyrufa-equivalent doesn't have to, after they've gathered their players, say 'Oh by the way, I run games with slavery and rape,' and now players might want to bail because to him it was a default assumption and to others it's a traumatic event. Sure, if you know you're playing with a friend who lost her eye to a dog mauling it can be a sensitive issue. But not everyone knows the personal history of everyone they game with and Anon4 doesn't have to stop the game after you introduce an eye-eating dog and explain why they have an issue with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are missing the point... I'm saying rats and spiders don't need to be on the list because they are covered by the fill in the blank option. And your argument that its on the list so you don't have to justify triggering people doesn't work because snakes and centipedes aren't on the list....<br /> <br /> Besides its a minor point, I'm giving constructive criticism on the form, it comes off as random to have rats and spiders on there.<br /> <br /> And I've said its useful as a tool for convention games, with the implication that its useful for games where you play with randos and strangers, and I specifically only gave my opinion concerning playing with friends. My points still stand you should talk with your players/prospective players and not just replace it with some bureaucratic form. And your missing the point if they have these consent forms on the table anyone can look at it and that's as revealing as stoping the game to say lets please not include dogs, and even more insidious because you don't even know someone has read that part of your form. Or you could just give it to the Game Master to hold onto, and that is fine with strangers but can be weird to have a list of all your friends' fears.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I don't think Nyrufa has at all said he includes scenes of Rape in his game, probably slavery because that is a ubiquitous fantasy trope, he just says his Orcs and Goblins in his world are the types of beings who do that. If I play Werewolf I don't need to depict scenes of the atrocities the Black Spiral Dancers do, but they can still have it established their Atrocities are well known and you don't want to be taken prisoner by them.<br /> <br /> Seriously people seem to be going out of their way to put words in Nyrufa's mouth...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:43:44-07:00","id":1336345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336338#post1336338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are easier ways to say &quot;I'm not going to discuss this in good faith.&quot; There are easier ways to say &quot;I'm okay with being part of the problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> We've been round this conversation circle a whole damn lot with you, and I think it's clear you're comfortable with your positions, which includes a lot of other people strongly objecting to yours. Sooooo what are you trying to do here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay I'm not familiar with Nyrufa's posts, is this something that has been argued with before this thread or is this just from this thread?<br /> <br /> And its a good point saying nothing you will say will change my mind is probably not something to say in a conversation like this, and even adding the word probably into it would fix a lot, but its not useful to say somebody is part of the problem when having a discussion with them. To me, that is literally the same level of &quot;as bad faithyness&quot; you prescribe to Nyrufa. It's probably satisfying to type, and you will get high fives from people that already agree with you but as part of a discussion it doesn't come off as charitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:48:17-07:00","id":1336346,"title":"","content":"Sexual assault doesn't have to occur &quot;on-screen&quot; for it to be triggering to players, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> - just flippantly mentioning the possibility of it happening is often enough to put some in a bad headspace.<br /> <br /> \u200bI know I wouldn't want to play in a Werewolf game in which our PCs would explicitly face torture if we were ever taken captive, <i>regardless </i>of whether or not the ST was going to give us a graphic description of it occurring or &quot;cut to black.&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:54:28-07:00","id":1336350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336316#post1336316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a very useful thing to say.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's a very useful thing to say if you want to protect people that want to use RPGs to be assholes to other people. Otherwise it's not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You shouldn't. It's a bad habit that directly stems from racist ideology.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, like I said. It's a cop out. You're abdicating your responsibility as an author to choose your words carefully to communicate your intended meaning to other people, and then getting defensive when they know what the word means to everyone else, rather than just what you've decided it should mean.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would vociferously object as both someone that cares about not being dumb with words - esp. in a first contact situation - and as a biologist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But you yourself said you want Orcs and Goblins that aren't nuanced or complex...this is nuance. If they are self-aware to know that they've being evil, and could choose to not be evil, then their evil is a moral failing no matter what their instincts, and they're not just savage monsters to have a power fantasy by killing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And that choice is a conscious act on your part, which is something everyone that has any interaction with your setting is within their rights to critique. Any stupid things you decide to encode into your setting is stuff people have every right to call out for being stupid, and more so because you yourself are the only person to blame for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, but the people that play it are, even you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This whole attitude is one of the reasons why we have things like this consent form in the first place. The general RPG world wants to claim their more than adult enough to not need these tools, but then want to wave incredibly immature thinking in other people's faces.<br /> <br /> We need consent tools because you sound - whether you intend to or not, or care or not - like the kind of person that would subject their players without warning or consent, to the graphic depictions of children being raped and then cannibalized, and then when everyone gets upset, you'd insist everyone but you is the problem.<br /> <br /> Someone that seriously says, &quot;there are no themes, stop reading into stuff,&quot; is someone who's only goal is to cause others emotional harm; and I absolutely believe that's true about the South Park creators. Because they said so. They just claim causing harm to as many people as possible somehow makes it OK.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1 - of course I'm not using it as an excuse for players to be ass holes to other people. That's absolutely ridiculous! If somebody at your table is spewing hate speech towards somebody in real life, then go ahead and deal with them. But if they're restricting such behavior to in character actions, and directing it towards other in game characters then that's perfectly fine.<br /> <br /> 2 - Bull shit, humans have been using the term &quot;race&quot; for thousands of years. What would you suggest we use to refer to each other as? Should we start identifying humans by various &quot;breeds?&quot; Because that sounds even worse!<br /> <br /> 3 - I'm against the idea of them being nuanced on a large scale. But I don't have any particular qualms about there being a rare outlier among their kind appearing once in a while. There's plenty of stories throughout fictional media that involve that very concept, usually with said outlier becoming an enemy of their own kind and fighting to oppose the evil they represent. As I said, when I use the word &quot;evil&quot; for describing a race, I do so in a context where evilness is ingrained into their very being. They can struggle against it, but they can never truly conquer that side of themselves.<br /> <br /> Take the dhampir, Blade for example. No matter how many vampires he destroys over the course of his life, he still has that craving for human blood, and only manages to suppress it through a daily use of special drugs. He might stand on the side of humanity, and he might hate the undead with a burning passion. But he is and will always be a monster, one who's inherent nature will always threaten the very people he tries to protect.<br /> <br /> <br /> 4 - No, it's not stupid, and anybody who follows the rule of Show Don't Tell is likely to agree. I'm not sure if you're aware of the controversy that surrounded the first episode of Goblin Slayer, but I was checking around for videos talking about it. What I found was one discussion in which they go on about how many stories often claim that the enemy of the story is an objective threat which needs to be destroyed, but they often shy away from proving that to be the case. Sure, the villains may be depicted as doing evil things from time to time, but such behavior fails to drive home the idea that this threat needs to be eradicated.<br /> <br /> Goblin Slayer addresses this idea, by going into graphic detail about why the protagonist has absolutely no empathy for the little green monsters. Those who haven't read the manga were probably shocked when he began clubbing baby Goblins to death in front of the Priestess. But during the Goblin Lord chapter, we see that even as infants, Goblins are just as prone to evil and chaos as their adult counterparts. The Goblin Lord was spared by a heroine who decided to take pity on him, when she saw him crying in terror as an infant. And the very second she turned her back to him and began to leave, the infant Goblin bashed her skull in with a rock!<br /> <br /> Once again, claiming that your villain is evil and expecting people to take it on faith is kind of a weak sell. You have to prove to people that your villain is evil, and explain why they can not be reasoned with. Having an established lore which depicts them as being Inherently malicious from birth is a good way to go about accomplishing that.<br /> <br /> Unless the narrative of the story is specifically focused on exploring philosophical world views, such as doing the wrong thing for the right reasons, I do not want to sympathize with the enemy. If they are my enemy, then the only thing I'm going to be focusing on is finding a way to bring them down, and then celebrating afterwards. If you want peaceful coexistence, send a diplomat with a gift basket. Not a party of adventurers who are armed to the teeth and looking for riches. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T15:54:47-07:00","id":1336351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336346#post1336346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sexual assault doesn't have to occur &quot;on-screen&quot; for it to be triggering to players, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> - just flippantly mentioning the possibility of it happening is often enough to put some in a bad headspace.<br /> <br /> \u200bI know I wouldn't want to play in a Werewolf game in which our PCs would explicitly face torture if we were ever taken captive, <i>regardless </i>of whether or not the ST was going to give us a graphic description of it occurring or &quot;cut to black.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be mentioned in the game is the point, the point is its in the corebook of a lot of games. I don't think you would be into playing Werewolf the Apocalypse Anyways, because that's literally the point of the Black Spiral Dancers, and there is no point in using them if you are going to whitewash their history to have them only be murderers.<br /> <br /> Exalted includes rape and slavery in its basic setting. So even if you don't include that in your game its in the setting unless you explicitly go out of your way to tell your players &quot;by the way I removed that all from the setting&quot;. Just don't include that stuff in the PC's journey if it triggers your players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:00:42-07:00","id":1336352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336345#post1336345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay I'm not familiar with Nyrufa's posts, is this something that has been argued with before this thread or is this just from this thread?<br /> <br /> And its a good point saying nothing you will say will change my mind is probably not something to say in a conversation like this, and even adding the word probably into it would fix a lot, but its not useful to say somebody is part of the problem when having a discussion with them. To me, that is literally the same level of &quot;as bad faithyness&quot; you prescribe to Nyrufa. It's probably satisfying to type, and you will get high fives from people that already agree with you but as part of a discussion it doesn't come off as charitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is to Nyru as &quot;i DuN LiKe t3h PuNk N' t3h PeRsOnAl HoRrOr iN mY vAmPiRe&quot; was to Cam.<br /> <br /> I've done this rodeo too many times to care, and I feel like Nyru has done this enough to know how this is going to go, which leaves me with just the question of &quot;Why the fuck are we doing this?&quot; Given the choice of just diving to that point and going through the usual bullshit, I will opt for the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:09:20-07:00","id":1336354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336339#post1336339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just describing what's wrong with discrimination, not what's specifically wrong with racism.<br /> <br /> To ask a probing question regarding your phrasing: Is holding racists beliefs bad even if you never actively do something racist? If someone thinks black people are bad, but never meets a black person to mistreat... is that neutral, or wrong?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. Just because something doesn't hurt someone doesn't mean it ain't wrong. <br /> <br /> Is there a point to this? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second you say something like, &quot;goblins are an evil race,&quot; you've made them an allegory for real world cultural issues. Maybe you avoid racism, or classism, or whatever, but &quot;race&quot; is a fictional concept humans made up as an excuse to be shitty to each other. When you call something in your fantasy world a &quot;race&quot; you're saying, &quot;you should consider these analogues to humans,&quot; and then people are going to be primed to look at the context you put in your setting. </div> </div> </div>Urm, no. Fantasy races are a thing. Its a limit of language. <br /> <br /> 1. Race was made up because of common features found, due to geographic isolation. Not because of 'excuse to be shitty to each other'. <br /> 2. What else do we call them? Fantasy breeds? Fantasy types? <br /> 3. No, when someone say 'Fantasy race', they mean 'Is sapient, and in a fantasy world'. Not 'You should consider these analogues to humans'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:11:05-07:00","id":1336356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336345#post1336345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay I'm not familiar with Nyrufa's posts, is this something that has been argued with before this thread or is this just from this thread?<br /> <br /> And its a good point saying nothing you will say will change my mind is probably not something to say in a conversation like this, and even adding the word probably into it would fix a lot, but its not useful to say somebody is part of the problem when having a discussion with them. To me, that is literally the same level of &quot;as bad faithyness&quot; you prescribe to Nyrufa. It's probably satisfying to type, and you will get high fives from people that already agree with you but as part of a discussion it doesn't come off as charitable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't go so far as to say it's an actual problem. More but rather it's more of a disagreement on whether or not making the &quot;monsters&quot; of the setting more nuanced by giving them free agency is a good idea. I obviously disagree with it, as I personally feel that defeats the very reason for calling them &quot;monsters&quot; in the first place. While others on the forum disagree with the idea that any sentient life form can be universally dedicated to one side of the alignment spectrum.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as I realize this discussion is veering quite far from the original topic. I want to say that I personally agree that players should receive proper warning about what kind of content the game is going to include, and to possibly alter it if it seems like it's going to be a major problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336352#post1336352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is to Nyru as &quot;i DuN LiKe t3h PuNk N' t3h PeRsOnAl HoRrOr iN mY vAmPiRe&quot; was to Cam.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Really mature of you, Arcane...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-17-2019, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:12:20-07:00","id":1336357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336343#post1336343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are missing the point... I'm saying rats and spiders don't need to be on the list because they are covered by the fill in the blank option. And your argument that its on the list so you don't have to justify triggering people doesn't work because snakes and centipedes aren't on the list....<br /> <br /> Besides its a minor point, I'm giving constructive criticism on the form, it comes off as random to have rats and spiders on there.<br /> <br /> And I've said its useful as a tool for convention games, with the implication that its useful for games where you play with randos and strangers, and I specifically only gave my opinion concerning playing with friends. My points still stand you should talk with your players/prospective players and not just replace it with some bureaucratic form. And your missing the point if they have these consent forms on the table anyone can look at it and that's as revealing as stoping the game to say lets please not include dogs, and even more insidious because you don't even know someone has read that part of your form. Or you could just give it to the Game Master to hold onto, and that is fine with strangers but can be weird to have a list of all your friends' fears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rats and spiders tend to be common monsters found in RPGs, which is likely why they're called out. You could have a blank spot for 'Animals' but saying it doesn't need to be on the list seems superfluous. It would make no difference if it said Centipedes and Snakes but they went with Rats and Spiders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I don't think Nyrufa has at all said he includes scenes of Rape in his game, probably slavery because that is a ubiquitous fantasy trope, he just says his Orcs and Goblins in his world are the types of beings who do that. If I play Werewolf I don't need to depict scenes of the atrocities the Black Spiral Dancers do, but they can still have it established their Atrocities are well known and you don't want to be taken prisoner by them.<br /> <br /> Seriously people seem to be going out of their way to put words in Nyrufa's mouth... </div> </div> </div>I appreciate you want to defend Nyrufa but its based off him saying, 'And I prefer my Orcs and Goblinoids to be slave trading, rape crazed barbarians.'<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not really directing any arguments against him because he hasn't expressed any stance regarding the sheet. But he has established a number of 'lines' that would fit on the sheet and they would probably pay to be set before the game starts rather than during play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-17-2019, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:23:24-07:00","id":1336359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336356#post1336356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wouldn't go so far as to say it's an actual problem. More but rather it's more of a disagreement on whether or not making the &quot;monsters&quot; of the setting more nuanced by giving them free agency is a good idea. I obviously disagree with it, as I personally feel that defeats the very reason for calling them &quot;monsters&quot; in the first place. While others on the forum disagree with the idea that any sentient life form can be universally dedicated to one side of the alignment spectrum.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as I realize this discussion is veering quite far from the original topic. I want to say that I personally agree that players should receive proper warning about what kind of content the game is going to include, and to possibly alter it if it seems like it's going to be a major problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see the issue then if you and the others agree that its important to having Trigger Warnings. Oiii internet squabbles make my head hurt.<br /> <br /> I have to say its one of my issues with DnD, I hate the morality system and the homogenous evil species. In games I'm fine with things like spirits hard coded to be evil, but if they are biological beings then I am more inclined to just have it be more the odds are stacked against them because they grow up in an overwhelmingly evil setting, rather then they have to be evil. So say you adopt an Orc or Goblin they can grow up to be good an Noble, or evil. They may have a biological aggressive streak but they have the potential to be nice. But you seem to agree acceptions can be made regardless of the nature of exceptions.<br /> <br /> I mean it seems like an artifact of days gone by that Half-Orcs are presented as default rather then just having Orcs in the core. And they whitewashed the implied heinous acts that spawned Half-Orcs (that an orc forced themselves on someone) and instead went out of their way to say noooo barbarian tribes sometimes have arranged Orc Human marriages. They should just have Orcs be the default rather then Half-Orcs, like how WoW does it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:23:28-07:00","id":1336360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336357#post1336357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rats and spiders tend to be common monsters found in RPGs, which is likely why they're called out. You could have a blank spot for 'Animals' but saying it doesn't need to be on the list seems superfluous. It would make no difference if it said Centipedes and Snakes but they went with Rats and Spiders.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bugs, Arachnids and Vermin would probably have been a more appropriate term, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:24:52-07:00","id":1336361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336356#post1336356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really mature of you, Arcane...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, are you perhaps suggesting that I should present my material in a way that is mindful of how it might affect you or other people even if I don't personally understand why you're offended by it, and maybe perhaps consider the reasons why it would come across that way? Because at this moment, I just assumed you'd be okay with that presentation.<br /> <br /> *COUGH*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:31:05-07:00","id":1336364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336359#post1336359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't see the issue then if you and the others agree that its important to having Trigger Warnings. Oiii internet squabbles make my head hurt.<br /> <br /> I have to say its one of my issues with DnD, I hate the morality system and the homogenous evil species. In games I'm fine with things like spirits hard coded to be evil, but if they are biological beings then I am more inclined to just have it be more the odds are stacked against them because they grow up in an overwhelmingly evil setting, rather then they have to be evil. So say you adopt an Orc or Goblin they can grow up to be good an Noble, or evil. They may have a biological aggressive streak but they have the potential to be nice. But you seem to agree acceptions can be made regardless of the nature of exceptions.<br /> <br /> I mean it seems like an artifact of days gone by that Half-Orcs are presented as default rather then just having Orcs in the core. And they whitewashed the implied heinous acts that spawned Half-Orcs (that an orc forced themselves on someone) and instead went out of their way to say noooo barbarian tribes sometimes have arranged Orc Human marriages. They should just have Orcs be the default rather then Half-Orcs, like how WoW does it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The main reason that I see people arguing against the morality system seems to often boil down to people aren't robots who are compelled to act in accordance with a specific set of principles. And to this, I would somewhat agree. However, this in absolutely no way means that the alignment system should be tossed out completely.<br /> <br /> I view the alignment spectrum as a set of guidelines for helping to establish your character's personality. Instead of being hard coded into your character, they influence how your character would normally choose to respond to a given situation. While changing somebody's alignment is possible, it shouldn't be as easy as Light Side, Dark Side is for Star Wars.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oops, I acted on impulse, instead of allowing wisdom to guide me. Guess I'm a Sith, now!&quot;<br /> <br /> Changes to one's alignment should be a gradual process that occurs over the course of the story. The character is routinely faced with situations that lead to them questioning their own morality and ethical world views. Ultimately leading up to them perceiving the world in a brand new way that falls in line with their new alignment. And this change should be restricted to a maximum of 2 alignment shifts per character during the entire campaign. Any player who tries to shift alignments a third time should just become Chaotic Neutral by default, since I imagine their mentality would be too fractured after that to truly believe in any sense of right or wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-17-2019, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:33:37-07:00","id":1336365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336361#post1336361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, are you perhaps suggesting that I should present my material in a way that is mindful of how it might affect you or other people even if I don't personally understand why you're offended by it, and maybe perhaps consider the reasons why it would come across that way? Because at this moment, I just assumed you'd be okay with that presentation.<br /> <br /> *COUGH*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Assuming that made up quote was supposed to represent me, typing it in all caps and writing it in &quot;1337&quot; speak was completely uncalled for.<br /> <br /> You don't see me disrespecting anyone here in such a fashion, do you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:35:23-07:00","id":1336366,"title":"","content":"Ooookay. I\u2019m going to take a quick hop back to the \u201cOP\u201d of this argument and see if I\u2019m inferring right what the blatant gap in mutual understanding is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336105#post1336105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the topic of racism, religion and cultural issues, I'd green light that in the case of fantasy context. Nobody is actually getting triggered when the light skinned High Elves and dark skinned Drow try to kill each other on sight. And I prefer my Orcs and Goblinoids to be slave trading, rape crazed barbarians. But if a player decides to start spewing obscenities at real world cultures and ethnic groups, then I'd start making sure I was out of punching distance, before things escalated.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what I\u2019m guessing here is that you\u2019re assuming a certain level of distance between how bigotry in D&amp;D-and-similar is portrayed and how it plays out IRL. As long as that distance is maintained, and in my experience it usually is, then you\u2019re right that it\u2019s pretty unlikely to cause any problems. If that distance <i>isn\u2019t</i> maintained though then things are quite likely to get very awkward very fast. Therefore, should you ever hypothetically use a topic checklist or have an equivalent pregame discussion, my recommendation is to make sure to explain the difference (as you see it) between \u201cfantasy\u201d and \u201creal\u201d racism and ask for a separate response on each. After all, half the point of this sort of book is to help you make sure everyone\u2019s on the same page on exactly this sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:37:07-07:00","id":1336368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336364#post1336364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The main reason that I see people arguing against the morality system seems to often boil down to people aren't robots who are compelled to act in accordance with a specific set of principles. And to this, I would somewhat agree. However, this in absolutely no way means that the alignment system should be tossed out completely.<br /> <br /> I view the alignment spectrum as a set of guidelines for helping to establish your character's personality. Instead of being hard coded into your character, they influence how your character would naturally choose to respond to a given situation. While changing somebody's alignment is possible, it shouldn't be as easy as Light Side, Dark Side is for Star Wars.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oops, I acted on impulse, instead of allowing wisdom to guide me. Guess I'm a Sith, now!&quot;<br /> <br /> Changes to one's alignment should be a gradual process that occurs over the course of the story. The character is routinely faced with situations that lead to them questioning their own morality and ethical world views. Ultimately leading up to them perceiving the world in a brand new way that falls in line with their new alignment. And this change should be restricted to a maximum of 2 alignment shifts per character during the entire campaign. Any player who tries to shift alignments a third time should just become Chaotic Neutral by default, since I imagine their mentality would be too fractured after that to truly believe in any sense of right or wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My issue is the whole land of the hats trope, were you have whole species of Klingon and Saiyajins. If you go to Rome or Sparta or Okinawa or Nazi Germany the lot of them wouldn't view themselves as evil, they just have a morality were they don't consider empathy for the other. A lot of people would have Lawful Good but be apart of a mighty brutal society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:40:41-07:00","id":1336369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336365#post1336365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Assuming that made up quote was supposed to represent me, typing it in all caps and writing it in &quot;1337&quot; speak was completely uncalled for.<br /> <br /> You don't see me disrespecting anyone here in such a fashion, do you?</div> </div> </div> </div>See this is my point I walk into this thread not knowing there was some sort of history between posters. I see Nyrufa just disagreeing with people and I see the others explode when directing at Nyrufa. How am I supposed to take it when I see one side of a discourse show blatant disdain and disrespect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:43:05-07:00","id":1336371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336366#post1336366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooookay. I\u2019m going to take a quick hop back to the \u201cOP\u201d of this argument and see if I\u2019m inferring right what the blatant gap in mutual understanding is:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So what I\u2019m guessing here is that you\u2019re assuming a certain level of distance between how bigotry in D&amp;D-and-similar is portrayed and how it plays out IRL. As long as that distance is maintained, and in my experience it usually is, then you\u2019re right that it\u2019s pretty unlikely to cause any problems. If that distance <i>isn\u2019t</i> maintained though then things are quite likely to get very awkward very fast. Therefore, should you ever hypothetically use a topic checklist or have an equivalent pregame discussion, my recommendation is to make sure to explain the difference (as you see it) between \u201cfantasy\u201d and \u201creal\u201d racism and ask for a separate response on each. After all, half the point of this sort of book is to help you make sure everyone\u2019s on the same page on exactly this sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Precisely, and I'm frustrated that it's proving difficult to clarify that to everyone.<br /> <br /> Thank you, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:43:28-07:00","id":1336372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336365#post1336365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Assuming that made up quote was supposed to represent me, typing it in all caps and writing it in &quot;1337&quot; speak was completely uncalled for.<br /> <br /> You don't see me disrespecting anyone here in such a fashion, do you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that leads to a clarification-NO, that was not you, that was Cam. Also, it wasn't all caps, it was in the vein of that Mocking Spongebob meme.<br /> <br /> Mind you, your persistence on the subject is getting me close to thinking of your arguments in that format, and considering that Cam's was just about taste and yours regards how to treat people, this is marking you worse. <b><u>AND YES</u></b>, I do see you doing the same thing when you dismiss Arms' completely out of hand, particularly when you try to tell him, real actual Jew, how Jewish coding in fiction either isn't a thing or that it isn't affecting anything, which is an unfortunately common behavior for you. The looser and more generic arguments such as that surrounding the problems of declaring a fictional race evil carries that disrespect.<br /> <br /> But anyways, you've dodged two of my questions. Currently, I don't expect you to answer them because I imagine it's uncomfortable, where as the rest of my commentary is easier to go after. Feel free to prove me wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-17-2019, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:50:42-07:00","id":1336373,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think using the word &quot;fantasy races&quot; means that those fantasy races should be viewed as analogous to ideas involving race in the real world.<br /> <br /> That said, going back to the thread topic, if someone is getting triggered by the words &quot;fantasy race&quot; because when they hear race they start thinking about real-world racism, then what would be a good word to use instead? Fantasy breeds? Fantasy species? Fantasy creatures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:51:20-07:00","id":1336375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336372#post1336372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do see you doing the same thing when you dismiss Arms' completely out of hand, particularly when you try to tell him, real actual Jew, how Jewish coding in fiction either isn't a thing or that it isn't effecting anything, which is an unfortunately common behavior for you. The looser and more generic arguments such as that surrounding the problems of declaring a fictional race evil carries that disrespect.<br /> <br /> But anyways, you've dodged two of my questions. Currently, I don't expect you to answer them because I imagine it's uncomfortable, where as the rest of my commentary is easier to go after. Feel free to prove me wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, I didn't get the chance to point this out in the previous topic, because Charlaquin banned me from replying there. In an effort to avoid that happening here, I'm just going to give this ONE reply on the idea of &quot;Jewish&quot; coding...<br /> <br /> The fact that Tolkein had to outright state that the Dwarves of his setting were meant to be Jews, and that he was surprised that this wasn't an obvious conclusion for people to come to... means that the majority of people who saw his work did not think of the Jews in such offensive terms. Then people started raising a fuss about it, and suddenly people are thinking &quot;Oh, I guess this is how I should imagine portraying Jews from now on.&quot;<br /> <br /> And yet I'M the one being offensive, for not immediately associating them with a bunch of gold obsessed drunkards...<br /> <br /> <br /> There, that's my thoughts on the subject. I'm done discussing it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T16:59:50-07:00","id":1336378,"title":"","content":"In my experience, for the most part people tend to link dwarves much more to Ireland or Scotland than to Jews anyway (probably because so many dwarves have had various sorts of Irish/Scottish accents in media). While Tolkeen was definitely a racist asshole, the things he created have moved well outside the bounds of The Lord of the Rings, and I think it's possible to look at various fantasy races/breeds/creatures/whatever without necessarily having that heavily colored by what Tolkeen intended.<br /> <br /> These days, when people are thinking about dwarves in the Forgotten Realms or whatever, they're probably <i>not</i> thinking about dwarves as caricatures of Jews.<br /> <br /> *edit* Like, I know a lot of people who enjoy the Cthulu mythos. They've played various games (board games, video games, etc) but never read anything from Lovecraft.Lovecraft, of course, was incredibly racist, but there are tons of people who enjoy the mythos he created and many of them may have no idea that the guy who created that stuff was so racist.<br /> <br /> When they get into a discussion about Nyarlathotep or whatever pops up in their Call of Cthulu game, the racist shit that Lovecraft wrote has no real bearing on that because the material the players are reading has been filtered through other authors, screenwriters, etc, to the point that most of his racist ideas are no longer really there, unless people specifically go back to read the original source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-17-2019, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:00:42-07:00","id":1336379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336375#post1336375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, I didn't get the chance to point this out in the previous topic, because Charlaquin banned me from replying there. In an effort to avoid that happening here, I'm just going to give this ONE reply on the idea of &quot;Jewish&quot; coding...<br /> <br /> The fact that Tolkein had to outright state that the Dwarves of his setting were meant to be Jews, and that he was surprised that this wasn't an obvious conclusion for people to come to... means that the majority of people who saw his work did not think of the Jews in such offensive terms. Then people started raising a fuss about it, and suddenly people are thinking &quot;Oh, I guess this is how I should imagine portraying Jews from now on.&quot;<br /> <br /> And yet I'M the one being offensive, for not immediately associating them with a bunch of gold obsessed drunkards...<br /> <br /> <br /> There, that's my thoughts on the subject. I'm done discussing it!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're the one being offensive by, when presented with the fact that such presentation is problematic for people, saying , by way of Tolkien, &quot;that he was surprised that this wasn't an obvious conclusion for people to come to... means that the majority of people who saw his work did not think of the Jews in such offensive terms&quot; like that somehow stops the fact that it's offensive, like that <i>excuses</i> it from being offensive, and that as such you don't need to take the feelings of others on the matter with the same care and consideration you ask of me when I started mocking you.<br /> <br /> You were ignorant, and that could be excused. We're past that point now. When you continue in that vein regardless, you earn the disrespect of your peers. You may not like what you bought, but you sure as hell bought it.<br /> <br /> Noticed you still dodged the two questions I asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:08:59-07:00","id":1336381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336373#post1336373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, going back to the thread topic, if someone is getting triggered by the words &quot;fantasy race&quot; because when they hear race they start thinking about real-world racism, then what would be a good word to use instead? Fantasy breeds? Fantasy species? Fantasy creatures?</div> </div> </div> </div>How about \u201cmetatype?\u201d <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Yes that one\u2019s from a context in which they\u2019re all subspecies but I still like it.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336375#post1336375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that Tolkein had to outright state that the Dwarves of his setting were meant to be Jews, and that he was surprised that this wasn't an obvious conclusion for people to come to...</div> </div> </div> </div>Was he surprised? I got the impression that he deliberately went out of his way to mostly use centuries-to-millennia-old \u201ccode\u201d that contemporary readers would be less likely to immediately recognize, or at least that he shouldn\u2019t have been expecting them to recognize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 09-17-2019, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:13:22-07:00","id":1336384,"title":"","content":"Going assume these are the two questions you had for me. If not, please repeat them, and I'll answer them as best I can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336338#post1336338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are easier ways to say &quot;I'm not going to discuss this in good faith.&quot; There are easier ways to say &quot;I'm okay with being part of the problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> We've been round this conversation circle a whole damn lot with you, and I think it's clear you're comfortable with your positions, which includes a lot of other people strongly objecting to yours. Sooooo what are you trying to do here?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;I'm okay with being part of the problem&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>There is no problem.</b> People like you are imagining that there is a problem. That's why I refuse to &quot;discuss it in good faith.&quot; because I see it as a pointless endeavor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm sorry, are you perhaps suggesting that I should present my material in a way that is mindful of how it might affect you or other people even if I don't personally understand why you're offended by it, and maybe perhaps consider the reasons why it would come across that way? Because at this moment, I just assumed you'd be okay with that presentation.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I at least make the effort to think about how my side of the argument makes sense, so that I can convince the other side to acknowledge it's validity. Instead of resorting to childish mockery because I don't like the person I'm arguing with. I am happy to sincerely debate various topics, if I feel I have a strong opinion on the subject. But the only thing that comes out of acting like a bunch of grade schoolers, is the mods get called in to start thread banning people.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-17-2019, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:22:23-07:00","id":1336386,"title":"","content":"I've been debating with myself over whether I should even get involved in this long off-the-rails discussion. But now seems like a pretty good time to put this on the table.<br /> <br /> I cite Lindsay Ellis's video essay on Bright, specifically the section on Allegory and Coding (in a section called, funnily enough, &quot;Allegory and Coding&quot;). [Relevant section begins at <a href=\"https://youtu.be/gLOxQxMnEz8?t=1443\" target=\"_blank\">24:03</a>].<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gLOxQxMnEz8?t=1443\" data-code=\"gLOxQxMnEz8\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gLOxQxMnEz8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The important take-away being that, while Allegory is intentional, Coding is not, and crops up even when the author of a fictional/fantasy work didn't mean to. That just because a writer didn't intend a message does not mean a message isn't an applicable reading of the text. This being a direct result of the writer working within existing frameworks - including mythical or genre frameworks - without examining the assumptions with a critical eye, or considering how other people could read the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:29:25-07:00","id":1336387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336384#post1336384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I'm okay with being part of the problem&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>There is no problem.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I wish this wasn't as funny as it is. But it definitely got a laugh.<br /> <br /> Anyways, regarding the rest of it, the answer to the second question actually answers the first one, being that you're here to make convince other people of your argument<br /> <br /> Which, you know, fine, I get that, heaven forbid I try and deny that's what I do, but I mostly avoid topics like this for such purposes and just find a platform where I can spout my own opinion uncontested and let those who otherwise accept it come unto Arcane-'bout the only reason I got in here, and most other threads like it, was because I want to try and cut down on the clutter of circular conversation by getting the goals on the table. But that said, Okay, You're Here To Persuade People.<br /> <br /> I think you know by now who is Not Going To Be Persuaded, though, so Why Are You Wasting Your Time Like That?<br /> <br /> Don't feel like you need to answer that one. Do, however, feel free to answer that lingering second question of mine: &quot;are you perhaps suggesting that I should present my material in a way that is mindful of how it might affect you or other people even if I don't personally understand why you're offended by it, and maybe perhaps consider the reasons why it would come across that way?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, frankly if you're free to say what is and isn't a problem, surely I can disregard you saying that presenting you &quot;aS tAlKiNg LiKe tHiS&quot; is a problem just as much? I mean, after all,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336384#post1336384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>There is no problem.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-17-2019, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:38:53-07:00","id":1336390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336387#post1336387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think you know by now who is Not Going To Be Persuaded, though, so Why Are You Wasting Your Time Like That?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's hard to stop myself. By default, I don't really consider myself a politically active person. In fact, I like to think that I don't care about politics at all. But once I get started on a subject, I'm surprised by how easy it is for me to fixate on it. In fact, I've already forgotten how this argument started on this thread in the first place, and yet we just keep carrying on about it.<br /> <br /> Yes, I have no intention of changing my opinion on the subject, since I genuinely believe that I am right on this side of the argument, and you seem to feel the same way about your side. It seems the only way to resolve this debate would be if we both agree to drop the subject, and return to the OP's thoughts on consent in gaming.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">feel free to answer that linger second question of mine: &quot;are you perhaps suggesting that I should present my material in a way that is mindful of how it might affect you or other people even if I don't personally understand why you're offended by it, and maybe perhaps consider the reasons why it would come across that way?&quot;</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> <br /> You don't need to take their feelings into account. In fact, I suspect that the only way to prove to somebody that they're wrong is to apply a bit of brutal honesty in your argument. But it would do you credit to be more tactful in how you go about debating with somebody, if you want people to take you seriously.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:45:21-07:00","id":1336392,"title":"","content":"On topic:<br /> <br /> Consent, and formal ways of easily getting consent across, is important to games because we all have our problems, and we at the same time can't always know how those problems are going to manifest for other people. We should definitely try and intuit and empathize as much as we can in the first place, but clear communication helps to support those efforts, and starting on the premise of believing those with the problems when they clarify why it's a problem expands our understanding and gives us essential lenses for viewing the rest of the world. In time, some of those lenses may reveal themselves to only be quite particular, but in most cases they help to create a highly useful work station for ensuring that people feel comfortable working with us individiuals, and maybe even open them up to challenging their limits because they know they do so in a safe environment.<br /> <br /> So, things like the form in the OP are highly useful, and I really like them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T17:50:30-07:00","id":1336394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336390#post1336390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need to take their feelings into account. In fact, I suspect that the only way to prove to somebody that they're wrong is to apply a bit of brutal honesty in your argument. But it would do you credit to be more tactful in how you go about debating with somebody, if you want people to take you seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>IF &quot;You don't need to take their feelings into account&quot;, then why should<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Assuming that made up quote was supposed to represent me, typing it in all caps and writing it in &quot;1337&quot; speak was completely uncalled for.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>mean anything to me?<br /> <br /> Please tell me you understand the game you've set up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-17-2019, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T18:14:02-07:00","id":1336400,"title":"","content":"Because there\u2019s a difference between disagreeing with someone and mocking them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T18:16:48-07:00","id":1336402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336400#post1336400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there\u2019s a difference between disagreeing with someone and mocking them.</div> </div> </div> </div>True! But disregarding that this might be a problem simply because you don't believe it is a problem is basically the same level of dismissing them as mocking them is, so we've gone no where.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T18:17:58-07:00","id":1336404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336400#post1336400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there\u2019s a difference between disagreeing with someone and mocking them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Truth!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> As I said, nobody's going to take you seriously if you resort to posts like that. If you're goal is to convince them that they're wrong, you should conduct yourself in a more appropriate manner. If your goal is to just taunt them, then your input is not welcome, because you're contributing nothing to the conversation besides agitating those involved. Which can escalate it into something worse than it already is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T18:25:34-07:00","id":1336408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336404#post1336404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> As I said, nobody's going to take you seriously if you resort to posts like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You already told me your goal here isn't to be persuaded, but to persuade others. I already told you I don't waste time trying to persuade people who make that clear.<br /> <br /> What <i>I'm</i> doing is making an object lesson for other readers. You're my material.<br /> <br /> Or were. I'm done now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T18:28:52-07:00","id":1336410,"title":"","content":"Bump time:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336366#post1336366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what I\u2019m guessing here is that you\u2019re assuming a certain level of distance between how bigotry in D&amp;D-and-similar is portrayed and how it plays out IRL. As long as that distance is maintained, and in my experience it usually is, then you\u2019re right that it\u2019s pretty unlikely to cause any problems. If that distance <i>isn\u2019t</i> maintained though then things are quite likely to get very awkward very fast. Therefore, should you ever hypothetically use a topic checklist or have an equivalent pregame discussion, my recommendation is to make sure to explain the difference (as you see it) between \u201cfantasy\u201d and \u201creal\u201d racism and ask for a separate response on each. After all, half the point of this sort of book is to help you make sure everyone\u2019s on the same page on exactly this sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336371#post1336371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Precisely, and I'm frustrated that it's proving difficult to clarify that to everyone.<br /> <br /> Thank you, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it seems suspiciously like people missed this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T18:43:14-07:00","id":1336412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336408#post1336408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You already told me your goal here isn't to be persuaded, but to persuade others. I already told you I don't waste time trying to persuade people who make that clear.<br /> <br /> What <i>I'm</i> doing is making an object lesson for other readers. You're my material.<br /> <br /> Or were. I'm done now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the only thing you've taught me that nyfura is probably right. So... Congrats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T18:44:49-07:00","id":1336413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336410#post1336410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bump time:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since it seems suspiciously like people missed this.</div> </div> </div> </div>If people just read this summary it saves like a few pages of bickering. Just reading folks argue is exhausting.<br /> <br /> But this is an agreeable summary Sith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T18:53:06-07:00","id":1336415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336412#post1336412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the only thing you've taught me that nyfura is probably right. So... Congrats?</div> </div> </div> </div><u>I</u> definitely learned something, at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T19:03:28-07:00","id":1336416,"title":"","content":"My issue with the &quot;in a fantasy context&quot; argument is that it seems to suppose what happens in an imaginary context doesn't have to pass through the real minds of real people. I'm not talking about the DM's intent; I'm talking about the players' perceptions. An unreal thing gains a measure of reality when it is perceived by a real person, whether we're talking about imagination or empathy or paranoia or PTSD or any of the jillions of other permutations I'm excluding, so whether the DM treats it as a real thing is pretty much irrelevant to the experience of the person absorbing it.<br /> <br /> This hobby seems to attract a lot of mentally unhealthy and/or neurodiverse people* who process the world in ways the rest of y'all seem to find incomprehensible or even worthy of mockery. Resources like this sheet assist in clear communication so no one gets unwittingly hurt. I cannot imagine why a person would reject such a resource unless the goal is to continue hurting people while wanting to claim it was unwitting; and if you're offended by that because you think it's untrue, then please consider how that kind of proves my point about how unreal things can feel real to the person experiencing them.<br /> <br /> *or maybe that's just Americans in general, I don't really have enough international experience to say","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T19:28:25-07:00","id":1336425,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar271_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"271\" data-vbnamecard=\"271\">JimB</a> If the players have an OOC problem with certain content, then yes, a chart like that could prove helpful in setting up a campaign. In fact, I would suggest discussing said chart before actually working on the campaign at all, so that you don't accidentally find yourself having to rewrite something that was going to be in the game before you found out a player wasn't comfortable with it.<br /> <br /> But if the problem only exists within the contents of the IC personality, and everybody at the table seems cool with it, then I say &quot;go nuts!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T19:43:05-07:00","id":1336427,"title":"","content":"Whee... you go eat and boom...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336334#post1336334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude come on you don't need to make personal attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, if you think anything was a true personal attack, you should be reporting me to the mods. Second, I'd contest that phrasing, even if I'd be comfortable with the mods dinging me on the tone; spirit of the law instead of the letter of the law and all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You disagree with him, you don't need to call him his opinions stupid. </div> </div> </div>I called encoding a specific thing as a factual empirical truth in the setting as stupid. I stand by that. As I noted, it goes against his own stated desired outcome on top of my own personal objections to phrasing/wording. I can think an idea is stupid without it being an attack on the person that said it. My wife endures me saying stupid things all the time, and frequently calls attention to them (even if it's a more friendly exchange than this).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Very few people believe Dwarves are allegories to Hebrews in Lord of the Rings, even if it's true. Not everything is an allegory, otherwise, everything is an allegory and that isn't helpful... </div> </div> </div>OK, I know this is actually hard (because if varies significantly by language and culture and is really complicated) but in English please use Jew over Hebrew when talking about people; or perhaps Semitic if we're getting into the weeds of ancient/classical groups that were coexisting side by side (since the over lap of Jew and Hebrew gets messy at a few points in history).<br /> <br /> Also... I really don't care if &quot;very few people believe.&quot; It's both true, and something that's aimed at my person identity. Do you have so little empathy for me that my frustration with people that care more about playing D&amp;D without thinking about where D&amp;D tropes came from rather than recognize the painful past some of these things represent, is something you need to ask me to shut up about? My pain as insults to my people are ignored for other people to enjoy their games in ignorance or apathy is just a nuisance?<br /> <br /> Or do I have your permission to actually stand up for people not revising out anti-Semitic elements of history so they can claim they were never there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look Race is an outdated term and I don't think its useful to be included in RPGs, yet they have it already coded into the grammar. </div> </div> </div>And fortunately, we can change this. It wasn't actually that long ago that lots of things were acceptable things to say, that we know regard as slurs. It's just keeping the pressure up for people to change.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336350#post1336350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - of course I'm not using it as an excuse for players to be ass holes to other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. But you're missing the point of how you're saying what you're saying. Whatever you mean, or do in your personal life, doesn't change how you sound to me based on the words you pick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if they're restricting such behavior to in character actions, and directing it towards other in game characters then that's perfectly fine. </div> </div> </div>No, this is definitely something that should be discussed ahead of time. Not everyone wants to play in games where slurs are used, even if exclusively in-character (or whatever other poor behavior). Not everyone wants to play in darker games (either ever or all the time) and have to deal with such matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bull shit, humans have been using the term &quot;race&quot; for thousands of years. What would you suggest we use to refer to each other as? Should we start identifying humans by various &quot;breeds?&quot; Because that sounds even worse! </div> </div> </div>Um, the word &quot;race&quot; as a more general concept similar to ethnicity is around 500 years old. The modern definition of race as distinct categories of humans that are not base purely on national, linguistic, cultural, or genetic markers is less than 200 years old. We are talking about an English word... modern English is only around 600 years old... we can't have been using the word for thousands of years if it hasn't existed for more than a few centuries.<br /> <br /> Ideally, we'd just call people... people... as radical of a thought as that is. Nothing supports the idea of there being distinct subspecies of humans that require differentiation in these terms.<br /> <br /> Ideal world not existing, we should balance factual groupings and self-identifiers. Race should only really be used when defending people from discrimination based on the perceptions of race as a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure if you're aware of the controversy that surrounded the first episode of Goblin Slayer,... </div> </div> </div>I've actually watched the whole series so.... yeah. Goblins aren't really called a race in it though. They're just a monster type.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Goblin Slayer addresses this idea, by going into graphic detail about why the protagonist has absolutely no empathy for the little green monsters. </div> </div> </div>Goblin Slayer is a very good way to prove that &quot;less is more&quot; is something to keep in mind. It establishes these things a few dozen times more than it needs to; and the anime is less graphic than the source material... I mean, things like the fact that they use poisons that keep working despite healing magic because the healing magic just traps the poison in the sealed up wounds is plenty to establish them as clever and gruesome without showing them trying to rape someone, or using the shadows on the wall trick to make it clear what they're doing to a corpse. The bigger thing that's important to establish for the setting and story is not how evil they are, but that in the setting that letting any of them live results in them getting upgraded to higher level bad guys to establish why Goblin Slayer is so genocidal.<br /> <br /> Of course, goblins being really horrible isn't even the point of the story. The point of the story is how dumb glory seeking adventuring is, and is a deconstruction of the RPG/fantasy tropes of 'starting level' monsters that are dangerous enough you constantly need people going out to fight them, but then they level up and go fight bigger baddies, and leave those early threats around. If all of the high level characters in the setting got together, they could probably wipe out goblins in a few days (esp. if they listen to Goblin Slayer on tactics), but none of them care to &quot;stoop&quot; to the level of fighting something so beneath them as goblins.<br /> <br /> The deities of the setting are literally portrayed as sitting around influencing the world by.... rolling dice in games. One of the tag lines for the main character is, &quot;He doesn't let people roll the dice,&quot; because of his rebellion against the default order of his world.<br /> <br /> Goblin Slayer is not subtle. Goblins are horrible monsters. But the real villians are the indifferent beings sitting above it all, unleashing suffering on people for their entertainment... and that would be us the players of RPGs. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336375#post1336375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that Tolkein had to outright state that the Dwarves of his setting were meant to be Jews, and that he was surprised that this wasn't an obvious conclusion for people to come to... means that the majority of people who saw his work did not think of the Jews in such offensive terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>To correct this, he was surprised that people were asking to confirm it 30 years after the books came out, and a lot of the context that was more clear during their release was changed by WWII.<br /> <br /> As well, Tolkien thought he was representing Jews in a positive fashion through his dwarves. He was clearly angry at people comparing his use of dwarves (who he felt were a noble people fallen from their former glory) to the Nazis using Germanic dwarves as anti-Semitic stereotypes; even if he never had a recorded letter or statement to address the whole gold lust issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336354#post1336354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a point to this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Primarily? To establish that your phrasing of active discrimination was not your sum total of what's wrong with bigotry. Since it's not, there's not much more as that's clear. Mostly from here, it's that if you acknowledge that racism, even just in thought, is bad, then racism is hard to defend in text just because it's become normalized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Urm, no. Fantasy races are a thing. Its a limit of language. </div> </div> </div>Fantasy races largely stem from early modern fantasy writers wanting to have them as allegory; since they're not there to represent their origins in myth for no other narrative reason. Tolkien wanted you to identify elves, dwarves, hobbits, and even orcs as humans; even if orcs are corrupted by evil forces they started as elves and all. The whole point was to use language that (at the time) to make it easier to see them as identifiable instead of alien.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Race was made up because of common features found, due to geographic isolation. Not because of 'excuse to be shitty to each other'. </div> </div> </div>Race is a modern concept, not just the general nature of humans to look for patterns and name them. And... what do you think people were coming up with new ways to divide humans into different categories were up to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. What else do we call them? Fantasy breeds? Fantasy types? </div> </div> </div>I'd rather see it be specialized to the setting to reflect how they're being used in that setting. Species works for me if we need a more general one for D&amp;D style fantasy, but type isn't bad. Creatures might work but seems a bit mixed on the &quot;impersonal&quot; issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. No, when someone say 'Fantasy race', they mean 'Is sapient, and in a fantasy world'. Not 'You should consider these analogues to humans'. </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's what D&amp;D encouraged by pulled them out of the context of the writers that came up with them. This goes back to the whole, &quot;is racism bad even if you don't do anything racist&quot; thing. Pulling racist (or other -ist) tropes from fantasy and making a game out of them that doesn't include the original context doesn't mean you've eliminated the association. D&amp;D races might not be actively racist, but they're built on racist tropes that aren't completely gone, and they're still called races. So in the end, it's both.<br /> <br /> Though really, the whole idea of &quot;sapient&quot; is such hair splitting it's kinda ridiculous. We call ourselves <i>Homo sapiens</i> for a reason. Sapience is part of what we consider special about or species, and making fictional sapient species is imbuing them with a quality of &quot;humanness,&quot; just like race is something we only use to talk about other humans and calling them races is asking for them to be looked as as having human qualities. Sapient is just a word for, &quot;we can identify with them because they're smart like we are,&quot; in this context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T19:57:51-07:00","id":1336430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336410#post1336410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it seems suspiciously like people missed this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less missed and more folded into the existing discussion.<br /> <br /> As JimB covered, the whole idea that fantasy equates to inherent separation isn't really a thing once people imagine experiencing something in their real brains.<br /> <br /> Yes, the whole point of this is why we should be building up our consent tools is well stated. But at the same time, minorities aren't really looking to be told, &quot;well the majority of people are fine as long as we call it fantasy, so you probably don't have to worry about it.&quot; If most people responded to fantasy racism like real world racism... we probably would be having a lot of this discussion. It's highlighting that a significant minority of people do experience fantasy racism as they do real world racism, and thus something that's not some strange outlier is important to remembering what to discuss in terms of consent tools, and how to phrase them. A consent form that asks me to differentiate between &quot;fantasy racism,&quot; and &quot;real racism,&quot; is kinda useless, because I'm someone that's had his people represented in a bigoted fashion by fantasy tropes. They're the same thing to me. Yes, I know you mean a more nuanced and longer concept for each in this, but if that doesn't make in onto a form or into a conversation, than it doesn't get discussed properly and the tool fails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:04:11-07:00","id":1336431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336427#post1336427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK. But you're missing the point of how you're saying what you're saying. Whatever you mean, or do in your personal life, doesn't change how you sound to me based on the words you pick.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How I sound to you is about as valid an argument as how I sound to a paranoid conspiracy theorist. If I say there are no underlying themes in my narrative, then there are no underlying themes in my narrative. I can not control what you choose to take away from my work, but no amount of slander is going to make it any more true. You are simply imagining things, plain and simple.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No, this is definitely something that should be discussed ahead of time. Not everyone wants to play in games where slurs are used, even if exclusively in-character (or whatever other poor behavior). Not everyone wants to play in darker games (either ever or all the time) and have to deal with such matters. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Right, I've outright agreed with and even stated this very stance on the issue several times here already.<br /> <br /> I said in my original post here that my DEFAULT stance on mature settings is R-rated. Default by no means signifies I'm not willing to play other types of games.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-17-2019, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:11:13-07:00","id":1336433,"title":"","content":"Because referring to an entire society of elf/dwarf/wookie/vulcan/old one/decepticon as a species isn't dehumanizing at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:20:50-07:00","id":1336436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336346#post1336346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sexual assault doesn't have to occur &amp;quot;on-screen&amp;quot; for it to be triggering to players, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - just flippantly mentioning the possibility of it happening is often enough to put some in a bad headspace.<br /> <br /> \u200bI know I wouldn't want to play in a Werewolf game in which our PCs would explicitly face torture if we were ever taken captive, <i>regardless </i>of whether or not the ST was going to give us a graphic description of it occurring or &amp;quot;cut to black.&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve had some Werewolf STs take the game to some really gross places without checking in with the players, and then either not pick up on or not care about when the players started giving pretty clear \u201cnot cool with this\u201d signals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:24:23-07:00","id":1336440,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> Okay first of all while I didn't grow up in a religious Family I'm Jewish/Roman Catholic by blood, but what because I never had a first communion or a bar mitzvah am I completely irrelevant in this conversation because family members died before I got important cultural touchstones and rituals bestowed upon me? You are presumptious, and you are acting elitist and like you are an arbitor of purity. I shouldn't have to state my real life background to have any opinion or validity in this conversation. I shouldn't have to state that I'm hapa to have any sort of say in public forums. Its disgusting to have to do so. Though at least nobody here has gone so far as to demand pictures of my skin being brown like they have done on Reddit or Sufficient Velocity.<br /> <br /> People are disagreeing with your very specific and contrived opinions. You are oversimplifying anything that doesn't agree with that is said here and you are telling other people what they mean by their own words. That comes off as an excessively righteous, bourgeois, elitist who disregards any opinion that dissents with your own.<br /> <br /> And I think its a stupid game to report people on argument threads like these, feel free to employ such tactics if you wish for some reason people seem to outright goad me into reporting them after I consistently point out I don't do that.<br /> <br /> When you go out and tell people what they think, and that they interpret their own thoughts wrong, that comes off from an outside perspective as off putting and revolting, unless they specifically jump on board out of tribalism. And that is what this is purity testing and tribalism.<br /> <br /> You can't stand people disagreeing with you, a number of people here can't stand any dissenting opinion. When a lot of people don't want to get involved in feeding hobbies to the monster of political agenda. You can't make games and hobbies only about politics. So far everyone here agreed its a good idea to communicate with your players and make sure everyone is comfortable with how they play the game and to not disrespect people. But that is not enough you have to get on a soap box and demand people tow the party line. You have to be divisive just for the sake of refining your own political currency. Its not enough people are moderate they have to be on your side of the line, oh but wait its not enough that they are on you side of the political divide because they are not close enough.<br /> <br /> This thread is about talking about consent in gaming and what people are comfortable with at the table, and people here are using it for pure egotistical purposes. You shouldn't act like bullies, even if you don't respect who you are talking to, and if you do people will judge you accordingly. And if you pout when they do so it doesn't change peoples minds. I didn't consent to have my personal identity used against. I don't care if people use the words jew or Hebrew, tone matters more then that. I cringe when people use the term oriental when describing someone but that water off a ducks back to me because it is more a sign of ignorance than malice. But I am supremely offended each time I have to defend my ethnic purity to people online. I shouldn't have to, people shouldn't weaponize that crap. I shouldn't have to state my ethnicity to a bunch of anonymous inquisitors online. I hate that, I get enough of that on Reddit.<br /> <br /> I find this disgusting. People are disagreeing online, honestly who cares about that. But when you start showing disdain for people for not agreeing with you enough and precisely in a specific way, that comes off as repugnant to a sober mind. Its as if so many of you do not deign to speak with anyone you deem below you in real life, and I doubt that could be true, few are so affluent or cut off where they can afford to just show such naked contempt for others on a daily basis in a community.<br /> <br /> But does it matter if I get triggered when my perceived identity is used against me? Apparently not if I'm not backed by a sizeable group of people.<br /> <br /> I hate this whole othering people that don't agree with you enough mentality.<br /> <br /> The mods don't care when their friends pile on people. I don't like people being bullied into towing the party line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:38:39-07:00","id":1336447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336440#post1336440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mods don't care when their friends pile on people. I don't like people being bullied into towing the party line.</div> </div> </div> </div>HAHAHAHA I'm one more offense away from getting a permaban despite being friends with a large number of mods, what is this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:41:47-07:00","id":1336449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336447#post1336447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HAHAHAHA I'm one more offense away from getting a permaban despite being friends with a large number of mods, what is this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't occur to you at all that if you weren't friends with the mods you would have already been banned long ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:41:59-07:00","id":1336450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336375#post1336375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, I didn't get the chance to point this out in the previous topic, because Charlaquin banned me from replying there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re either thinking of someone else, or you\u2019ve been holding on to this for a while, cause I haven\u2019t been a mod here for like three months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:43:09-07:00","id":1336451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336427#post1336427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primarily? To establish that your phrasing of active discrimination was not your sum total of what's wrong with bigotry. Since it's not, there's not much more as that's clear. Mostly from here, it's that if you acknowledge that racism, even just in thought, is bad, then racism is hard to defend in text just because it's become normalized.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fantasy races largely stem from early modern fantasy writers wanting to have them as allegory; since they're not there to represent their origins in myth for no other narrative reason. Tolkien wanted you to identify elves, dwarves, hobbits, and even orcs as humans; even if orcs are corrupted by evil forces they started as elves and all. The whole point was to use language that (at the time) to make it easier to see them as identifiable instead of alien.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Race is a modern concept, not just the general nature of humans to look for patterns and name them. And... what do you think people were coming up with new ways to divide humans into different categories were up to?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd rather see it be specialized to the setting to reflect how they're being used in that setting. Species works for me if we need a more general one for D&amp;D style fantasy, but type isn't bad. Creatures might work but seems a bit mixed on the &quot;impersonal&quot; issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, that's what D&amp;D encouraged by pulled them out of the context of the writers that came up with them. This goes back to the whole, &quot;is racism bad even if you don't do anything racist&quot; thing. Pulling racist (or other -ist) tropes from fantasy and making a game out of them that doesn't include the original context doesn't mean you've eliminated the association. D&amp;D races might not be actively racist, but they're built on racist tropes that aren't completely gone, and they're still called races. So in the end, it's both.<br /> <br /> Though really, the whole idea of &quot;sapient&quot; is such hair splitting it's kinda ridiculous. We call ourselves <i>Homo sapiens</i> for a reason. Sapience is part of what we consider special about or species, and making fictional sapient species is imbuing them with a quality of &quot;humanness,&quot; just like race is something we only use to talk about other humans and calling them races is asking for them to be looked as as having human qualities. Sapient is just a word for, &quot;we can identify with them because they're smart like we are,&quot; in this context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why yes, something may or may not have racist associations. <br /> <br /> So? <br /> <br /> Was the writer intending it to be racist. Were a writer say, make evil goblins or evil orcs, is he saying in his mind 'mwahahahhaha, I made them crude, savage, and stone tech users! That's coding for primitive savages which are primarily dark skinned! Racism quota, complete!'? Or is he just thinking 'Now, I need to make a race that's symbolises brutality and savagery. Usage of stone tools, strong physiques, as well as more unsophisticated language would bring in the message.' <br /> <br /> Sure, the savage hordes of monsters usually come from the mongols, and other swarthy men who come riding in horses to set cities on fire, but by this point, they've pretty much become their own thing. <br /> <br /> Tl; dr. It may have started racist, it may have racist associations, but it isn't racist to use the trope and fantasy archetype in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:44:03-07:00","id":1336453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336433#post1336433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because referring to an entire society of elf/dwarf/wookie/vulcan/old one/decepticon as a species isn't dehumanizing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah its clinical, that is why I choose between terms like civilization for some descriptions or species for others if it fits the theme, like a space game. But I've learned to not care if race is used for fantasy games, its specifically different from humanity being divided into races because fantasy games usually have Humans just be the human race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:45:45-07:00","id":1336454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336440#post1336440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> I cringe when people use the term oriental when describing someone</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, genuine question here: is &quot;oriental&quot; a racial slur? Because when I was growing up, everybody just used it as a word for Asians, so that's how my brain learned to internalize the definition. Is there some reason why it offends people to use this word?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You\u2019re either thinking of someone else, or you\u2019ve been holding on to this for a while, cause I haven\u2019t been a mod here for like three months.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Odd, I thought it was you. Then again, I have a crap memory, so chances are that it was somebody else. Sorry if I got you confused.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:46:11-07:00","id":1336455,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> sometimes a race of savage cannibals is just a race of savage cannibals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:48:16-07:00","id":1336457,"title":"","content":"RE: What word do we use instead of \u201craces\u201d for the various humanoid fantasy species... how about \u201cpeoples?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:50:24-07:00","id":1336458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336449#post1336449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't occur to you at all that if you weren't friends with the mods you would have already been banned long ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that I have been in situations where that sort relationship happened, have clear comparisons between mine and mods behaviors between those times, have a history of punishments here along with the clear understanding of how these things escalate here, and otherwise can point at the times when I stopped toeing the lines that directly led to responses?<br /> <br /> No. No, that thought never occured to me. I know <i>why</i> I get punished, and I <i>know</i> it's because I decided to stop playing nice by the forum standards.<br /> <br /> You'd be shocked and surprised to find out that we actually have really good mods here, and when I'm my worse self, I wish being friends with them came with perks like turning a blind eye to my shit. My worse self is not lucky like that.<br /> <br /> Don't conflate &quot;You don't like what I'm doing&quot; with &quot;Against community rules&quot;, as I have had to learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:52:52-07:00","id":1336459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336454#post1336454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, genuine question here: is &quot;oriental&quot; a racial slur? Because when I was growing up, everybody just used it as a word for Asians, so that's how my brain learned to internalize the definition. Is there some reason why it offends people to use this word?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Odd, I thought it was you. Then again, I have a crap memory, so chances are that it was somebody else. Sorry if I got you confused.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Orient was the term western people used for the east rather than say occident for the west. In general people developed aversions to using terms others applied to them rather then the terms they used for themselves, like Inuits being more appropriate then Eskimo (which means eater of raw flesh). But its so antiquated you don't hear it anymore and its a bit cringy but since its so antiquated and it comes off to me as innocent and I don't really care. I've been called full blown racial slurs out of hate, I don't care if someone says I'm oriental.<br /> <br /> Its like the term midget being used and popularized in common speech but by the time people grow into adults in the modern era we learn that its not polite to refer to someone as that, but honestly its not something people were really taught was wrong in a lot of places.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call Oriental a Slur, but its also probably not polite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:56:04-07:00","id":1336460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336457#post1336457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: What word do we use instead of \u201craces\u201d for the various humanoid fantasy species... how about \u201cpeoples?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I use Civilizations for intelligent species, or species to accentuate the alieness of a setting. It seems Race is more fitting in a fictional setting with actual nonhuman races then real life, where we are waiting for Dolphins to Evolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:56:15-07:00","id":1336461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336457#post1336457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: What word do we use instead of \u201craces\u201d for the various humanoid fantasy species... how about \u201cpeoples?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Why Lothar you are a paragon of the human peoples&quot; sounds silly.<br /> <br /> However ill offer up Kind as a stomach able alternative. Human Kind, Elven Kind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Don't poo poo an idea kids unless you got one of your own. 09-18-2019, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:56:39-07:00","id":1336462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336459#post1336459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eskimo (which means eater of raw flesh).</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know that, holy crap! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:57:10-07:00","id":1336463,"title":"","content":"Oriental is my favorite ramen flavor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:57:46-07:00","id":1336464,"title":"","content":"I see no reason why Oriental is a slur. I'm Chinese, and I see no issue with it. I simply consider it a facet of old-fashioned english. Like 'making love' or 'thee' or other words that have long since dropped out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:01:18-07:00","id":1336467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336463#post1336463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oriental is my favorite ramen flavor</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beef and Chicken aren't too bad either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:11:07-07:00","id":1336472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336430#post1336430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As JimB covered, the whole idea that fantasy equates to inherent separation isn't really a thing once people imagine experiencing something in their real brains.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not actually what anyone\u2019s argued. It\u2019s not that putting a fantasy coat of paint on realistic bigotry somehow makes it less relatable, it\u2019s that bigotry in fantasy settings is usually either so shallow and superficial as to lessen its realism or requires rejecting one or more of the setting\u2019s premises to be viewable as bigotry in the first place. The latter of which unarguably falls flat if the villain races/species are coded on anyone real, yes, but goblins, orcs, and kobolds aren\u2019t. And beholders and mind flayers definitely aren\u2019t either but funny how it\u2019s mostly only ever the humanoids that people object to not all being Alignment: Any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:14:03-07:00","id":1336474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336449#post1336449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't occur to you at all that if you weren't friends with the mods you would have already been banned long ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this? This is very much not true. There are a lot of people with whom the mods are very much not friends, who have been given just as many chances as Arc, if not more. They tend not to resort to permanent bans unless it is clear that the person is not amenable to changing their behavior. Look at how many suspensions Geckopirateship got before finally getting permabanned. Look how many times members of the mod team patiently explained to Camilla exactly why their posting behavior was problematic and what they could do to avoid getting banned before they eventually did. They were not friends with the mods. They lasted as long as they did because they looked like they were making an effort to change their behavior. The people who get banned quickly are the ones who make it abundantly clear that they have no intent to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:22:37-07:00","id":1336477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336460#post1336460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use Civilizations for intelligent species, or species to accentuate the alieness of a setting. It seems Race is more fitting in a fictional setting with actual nonhuman races then real life, where we are waiting for Dolphins to Evolve.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Civilizations is an ok one, although the term carries some colonialist baggage. Perhaps \u201cspecies\u201d for settings where they are indeed separate species and \u201ccultures\u201d or \u201cethnicities\u201d for settings where the differences are more akin to the variations between real-life groups of humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-18-2019, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:25:44-07:00","id":1336479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336461#post1336461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Why Lothar you are a paragon of the human peoples&amp;quot; sounds silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda like the sound of that, myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336461#post1336461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However ill offer up Kind as a stomach able alternative. Human Kind, Elven Kind</div> </div> </div> </div>Elvenkind sounds cool as a parallel to humankind for in-character speech. I was referring more to the rules term. \u201cChoose a Kind, Class, and Background\u201d sounds awkward to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:26:14-07:00","id":1336480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336472#post1336472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s not actually what anyone\u2019s argued. It\u2019s not that putting a fantasy coat of paint on realistic bigotry somehow makes it less relatable, it\u2019s that bigotry in fantasy settings is usually either so shallow and superficial as to lessen its realism or requires rejecting one or more of the setting\u2019s premises to be viewable as bigotry in the first place. The latter of which unarguably falls flat if the villain races/species are coded on anyone real, yes, but goblins, orcs, and kobolds aren\u2019t. And beholders and mind flayers definitely aren\u2019t either but funny how it\u2019s mostly only ever the humanoids that people object to not all being Alignment: Any.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The furthest weight that the term &quot;humanoid&quot; carries with me is &quot;this species is roughly shaped like a human, and possesses human characteristics.&quot; Beyond that, nothing. It's not meant to represent any specific group of people, unless I explicitly state as much to the audience.<br /> <br /> Which I will probably never do, because I am not worldly enough to know about such peoples, and I'm too lazy to conduct a more thorough investigation on the subject. One reason I prefer fantasy settings to those of modern realism, is because I have the freedom to make up their culture from scratch. Any parallels it might have to real life culture is purely coincidental, and not the intentional comparison that others perceive it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:27:37-07:00","id":1336481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336477#post1336477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Civilizations is an ok one, although the term carries some colonialist baggage. Perhaps \u201cspecies\u201d for settings where they are indeed separate species and \u201ccultures\u201d or \u201cethnicities for settings where the differences are more akin to the variations between real-life groups of humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look man. Everything has baggage. You say civilisation has baggage? Culture and ethnicity too. What with Indian boarding schools and the various genocides of ethnicity. <br /> <br /> At some point, the word has been used to justify fucked up things. <br /> <br /> Just use whatever, as long as everyone agrees on it. Just kick out anyone being too creepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:31:39-07:00","id":1336482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336481#post1336481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look man. Everything has baggage. You say civilisation has baggage? Culture and ethnicity too. What with Indian boarding schools and the various genocides of ethnicity. <br /> <br /> At some point, the word has been used to justify fucked up things. <br /> <br /> Just use whatever, as long as everyone agrees on it. Just kick out anyone being too creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said it\u2019s ok, what do you want from me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:33:44-07:00","id":1336484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336479#post1336479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda like the sound of that, myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> Elvenkind sounds cool as a parallel to humankind for in-character speech. I was referring more to the rules term. \u201cChoose a Kind, Class, and Background\u201d sounds awkward to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really anything works<br /> &quot;Although the Elven Civilization had collapsed long ago the Race continued on as a nomadic Peoples forever roaming the blasted wasteland their Kind once called home.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> But if we are just going with just a rules term just go with Race, everything else is loaded with follow up terms. <br /> <br /> Example Ancestry, of who? Does being an ancestor of one person give me a bonus over another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Reasons 09-18-2019, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:34:35-07:00","id":1336485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336482#post1336482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said it\u2019s ok, what do you want from me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. Not you that was for everyone in the thread, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:43:34-07:00","id":1336487,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that I should probably lay out an ideological stance for me:<br /> <br /> Like, my own personal take on things, which includes beliefs and disbeliefs, tend to play second when I'm any sort of position of power concerning what a person experiences or not. Like, as a minor example, I think Christianity is horseshit and that it's continued presence in society contributes a fair amount to it's ills* and will happily shit talk it on the street after a warning-but if you give me someone who feels their faith is important to them as a part of my gaming group, I am neither going to play a character or run a game that is going to tread on that fact. Out of game, I'm going to find out more of what they're comfortable with, and I will play exactly to that hilt, but while I think there should be more free and open talk out of game than in-game, as a member of the party, I still feel it important to take care of the person in there. If, for any reason, the player's faith becomes a problem for the table at large and it isn't resolvable after a lot of out of game discussion and compromise on my part, I might then ask that person to leave the group,** but I'm not going to tread on that person's faith in anything that resembles a capacity of authority in game, and only push my luck as I feel is appropriate for the individual out of it.<br /> <br /> My problem with this conversation, as it's developed, is that this angle reads, no matter how you phrase it, as &quot;I don't care if someone tells me this hurts them or not, I don't want to have to adjust my behavior to accomodate that&quot; which really just reads as &quot;I will hurt you in this way if I want to.&quot; Regarding the specifics about fantasy racism and how it relates to real world problems as such, I'm always fascinated to learn where the ideas in my head came from and learning how to do things another way (not only because I'm keen of social awareness, but also this tends to lead to different and innovative fiction that might not even lose the power of archetypes, which I'm also really keen on), but for me the problems of &quot;Well, does this come from somewhere/is this a real thing?&quot; is less of a logistical reality to catalogue and more a failure to take responsibility for the fact that This Person Is In My Group And Therefore I Am Responsible For Taking Care of Them. Like, let's say I shared Nyru's opinion about how this isn't a problem.*** I would <i>still not make it a thing</i> in my games, because <i>you just don't do that shit</i>. It would still read to me like &quot;I care more about doing what I want then making sure you're all right&quot;, which reads &quot;I will hurt you in this way if I want to.&quot;<br /> <br /> I have a lot of intellectual argumentation, emotional empathy, and personal damage against pretty much anything that evokes that read. At best, I don't feel like courtesy stays on the table for people who make that statement into a hill. I feel like that forms a basic line for what constitutes an intolerance that must not be tolerated. It goes double for gaming groups, which I just straight regard as My Domain.<br /> <br /> When you're in a gaming group, you take care of each other. If you're not willing to do that, for any reason, you shouldn't be in a gaming group.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, this flat refusal of &quot;It's not a thing!&quot; is unimportant. If someone raises it as a concern, either take it seriously or seriously converse with that person that this table may not be right for them. Anything else reads terribly and shouldn't be done.<br /> <br /> *If anyone wants to discuss this, take it to another thread, please.<br /> **And, in fact, this has happened-had a friend Tony who started wielding his faith as character motivation that fucked things over in-game and attacked players out of game. It boiled over and I kicked him out of the group. He expected people to follow him! They did not.<br /> ***But being blunt, it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-18-2019, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:51:46-07:00","id":1336490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336474#post1336474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, this? This is very much not true. There are a lot of people with whom the mods are very much not friends, who have been given just as many chances as Arc, if not more. They tend not to resort to permanent bans unless it is clear that the person is not amenable to changing their behavior. Look at how many suspensions Geckopirateship got before finally getting permabanned. Look how many times members of the mod team patiently explained to Camilla exactly why their posting behavior was problematic and what they could do to avoid getting banned before they eventually did. They were not friends with the mods. They lasted as long as they did because they looked like they were making an effort to change their behavior. The people who get banned quickly are the ones who make it abundantly clear that they have no intent to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>^, oh dear god, <i>this</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T23:00:47-07:00","id":1336493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336431#post1336431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I say there are no underlying themes in my narrative, then there are no underlying themes in my narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize that... themes are part of a narrative? It's kinda what keeps it from just being a rambling recitation of random events and all that. Theme is the &quot;why&quot; all of the events in the plot matter to the audience. Without a theme, it's just a bunch of things that happened, and the audience goes, &quot;why did we just pay attention to that?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can not control what you choose to take away from my work,.... </div> </div> </div>You can... influence it significantly though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336454#post1336454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, genuine question here: is &quot;oriental&quot; a racial slur?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but it's incredibly impolite due to it's outdated presumptions, hence likely to be insulting anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336433#post1336433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because referring to an entire society of elf/dwarf/wookie/vulcan/old one/decepticon as a species isn't dehumanizing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... if the goal is to avoid them being interpreted as analogues for humans and thus not having them read into more than the author intends... a certain amount of dehumanization is going to happen in any of this?<br /> <br /> Also, sci-fi uses species all the time without it having the issue assumed here. Maybe the science lets it work where it wouldn't in fantasy, but no solution is perfect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336451#post1336451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tl; dr. It may have started racist, it may have racist associations, but it isn't racist to use the trope and fantasy archetype in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is what do you do once you know about the racist associations? If you know, then how can you use it without it being at least a bit racist? Shouldn't the moral thing to be doing to be finding some different way to approach the subject matter?<br /> <br /> How is it acceptable to defend racist tropes in your work once ignorance is gone? Should we be working to do better? Or fighting people pointing out that it's racist so we can act like we were back before someone pointed out the racist associations?<br /> <br /> At some point don't we stop giving the benefit of the doubt that including things with racist origins, or racist associations, by someone into their work and just call them out for it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336472#post1336472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not that putting a fantasy coat of paint on realistic bigotry somehow makes it less relatable, it\u2019s that bigotry in fantasy settings is usually either so shallow and superficial as to lessen its realism or requires rejecting one or more of the setting\u2019s premises to be viewable as bigotry in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure there's a real difference in practice. It's not like there's some &quot;depth&quot; to racism where it counts. The real world has shallow and superficial racism too. &quot;Light skinned = good, dark skinned = bad,&quot; is shallow... but very common racism in real life and in fantasy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The latter of which unarguably falls flat if the villain races/species are coded on anyone real, yes, but goblins, orcs, and kobolds aren\u2019t. </div> </div> </div>That very much depends on who's doing the coding. Though the kobolds thing is rather odd given that in their origin myths they're generally beneficial beings... making D&amp;D kobolds a rather divorced from things because they're something made up and given a name from an obscure-ish mythological spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And beholders and mind flayers definitely aren\u2019t either but funny how it\u2019s mostly only ever the humanoids that people object to not all being Alignment: Any. </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's pretty much exactly my point though... the more human something is, the more uncomfortable it makes people to do things like code it as purely evil, because the more human it is the more we're going to see ourselves in it on some level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336440#post1336440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay first of all while I didn't grow up in a religious Family I'm Jewish/Roman Catholic by blood, but what because I never had a first communion or a bar mitzvah am I completely irrelevant in this conversation because family members died before I got important cultural touchstones and rituals bestowed upon me?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I felt you were irrelevant to the conversation, why would I be responding to you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are presumptious, and you are acting elitist and like you are an arbitor of purity. </div> </div> </div>I presumed a bit about your knowledge the complexities about Jewish self-identification terminology because you used Hebrews like that; as it is hard to track as it varies wildly by language and country based on local cultural history on if the two are considered interchangeable, or if one's considering rude over the other. Otherwise I don't feel I presumed anything about you.<br /> <br /> I did get very frustrated with your comment, but oddly for many of the reasons you seem upset at me. I mean, you're presuming a shit ton about me in this post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I shouldn't have to state my real life background to have any opinion or validity in this conversation. </div> </div> </div>I never asked you to, or even demanded something that required you talking about it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People are disagreeing with your very specific and contrived opinions. You are oversimplifying anything that doesn't agree with that is said here and you are telling other people what they mean by their own words. That comes off as an excessively righteous, bourgeois, elitist who disregards any opinion that dissents with your own. </div> </div> </div>Care to be more specific with any examples? I mean, you were complaining about implied personal attacks, and bullying, but here you are throwing a bunch of slights around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think its a stupid game to report people on argument threads like these,... </div> </div> </div>The mods have directly asked people to report instead of engaging if you feel someone's violated the forum rules; which personal attacks are.<br /> <br /> It's not a game, it's how we've been asked to behave by the team that keeps this place running.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you go out and tell people what they think, and that they interpret their own thoughts wrong, that comes off from an outside perspective as off putting and revolting, unless they specifically jump on board out of tribalism. </div> </div> </div>I think I've been rather emphatic about things like &quot;this is how it feels when you say X,&quot; rather than, &quot;you mean to say X,&quot; or whatever variation. If you don't feel I mean that in good faith, I doubt I can really change your mind at this point, but it's hard to take this as valid criticism when it feels like you're telling me what I think based on not taking the wording I used seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that is not enough you have to get on a soap box and demand people tow the party line. </div> </div> </div>We're on... page 8 now? Of me defending what seems to be a thing that doesn't really need defending: fantasy isn't a panacea to avoid consent issues. This all started because I objected to the defense of something with, &quot;but fantasy context!&quot; and demonstrated why that's not really a defense. All of this acrimony is because of the assertion that the game being a fantasy game doesn't provide enough context to avoid talking about these things.<br /> <br /> How is that me getting on a soapbox and demanding people tow a line?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't consent to have my personal identity used against. </div> </div> </div>OK, very seriously, where is this coming from, I'm seriously confused why you think this, because I really don't like doing that to people and I didn't think I did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mods don't care when their friends pile on people. </div> </div> </div>I have no friends or enemies on the mod team. I'm sure a few are frustrated with me from years of dealing with me and all. If I'm piling on anyone, they're not going to pull their punches because of personal bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T23:19:41-07:00","id":1336496,"title":"","content":"One thing about themes:<br /> <br /> Themes are inherent to any creative process because, whether we try to put them in or not, we think certain ways about certain things and even internally reward or punish things, and so whenever we deal with subject matter, our individual takes will manifest in a variety of ways, even if it's simply giving a topic more time and others no time at all. Our unconscious interests bleed out into our every presentation, even down to how we walk.<br /> <br /> So you may not think you have themes, but there's is content to read, and that content carries ideas, and thus themes. The big difference of focusing on a theme is that you hold more control over the presentation that simply letting your biases show.<br /> <br /> And boy howdy, there's little more embarrassing than have your nasty little asides slip out in unexpected ways when you're so sure they'd never show.<br /> <br /> ANYWAYS, moral of the story is you can either control your meanings or have your meanings confine you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T23:27:41-07:00","id":1336498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336431#post1336431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I say there are no underlying themes in my narrative, then there are no underlying themes in my narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be being too literal here, but: if you say there are no underlying themes in your narrative, that only means you do not intend to have underlying themes in your narrative. Whether that's true depends on how you execute your intent AND how your execution is received; because fiction is a collaborative process between the writer and the reader, not an immaculate act of creation uninfluenced by the society you live in and the attitudes you marinade in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":".  Cleaned up some grammar. 09-18-2019, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T23:31:31-07:00","id":1336499,"title":"","content":"^Also that.<br /> <br /> A big reason people like to kill the author is so they can fill the silence themselves without any authoritative objection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T01:25:55-07:00","id":1336506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336498#post1336498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may be being too literal here, but: if you say there are no underlying themes in your narrative, that only means you do not intend to have underlying themes in your narrative. Whether that's true depends on how you execute your intent AND how your intent is received; because fiction is a collaborative process between the writer and the reader, not an immaculate act of creation uninfluenced by the society you live in and the attitudes you marinade in which has objective value separate from the perceptions of your audience.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My intent, as it were, is to create a setting in which we can completely forget about real life and immerse ourselves in a world that is fundamentally different from it. I can not fathom the mentality of people who believe that every act of media absolutely must be inspired by real world events somehow. It's like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3953_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3953\" data-vbnamecard=\"3953\">Dwight</a> said, &quot;sometimes a race of savage cannibals is just a race of savage cannibals.&quot;<br /> <br /> When I try to create a fantasy setting, real life is the absolute furthest thing from my mind. I might occasionally draw inspiration from it at certain points, but this inspiration is purely aesthetic and has no actual substance beyond visual similarities. For the most part, I make up the world and it's inhabitants from scratch, drawing upon ideas brewed from my own imagination. At absolutely no point am I trying to push forward some kind of political agenda, or make some kind of artistic statement about our world. I hate our world, and wish to spend as much time away from it as possible.<br /> <br /> If I spent all my energy worrying about whether or not certain groups found certain content in my stories to be offensive, I might as well not even bother creating anything in the first place. I should just stick to writing the most TV-Y7 rated, children's programming, where everybody holds hands and sings songs, and there is never any physical conflict because we are all friends here. And it would be the most boring, insufferable trash I've ever worked on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T01:36:29-07:00","id":1336507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336506#post1336506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can not fathom the mentality of people who believe that every act of media absolutely must be inspired by real world events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagination is nothing but memory divorced from context. Humans cannot imagine new things: we can only rearrange what we already know. Your cannibals come from somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T01:42:41-07:00","id":1336510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336507#post1336507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your cannibals come from somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They come from the depths of my vore fetish, which was developed after finding Beachfox's artwork. Not because a tribe of people in the real world partook of human flesh at some point in history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2019, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T02:04:48-07:00","id":1336515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336507#post1336507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagination is nothing but memory divorced from context. Humans cannot imagine new things: we can only rearrange what we already know. Your cannibals come from somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen the things little kids come up with?<br /> Also my cannibals are totes OC, do not steal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T02:09:17-07:00","id":1336516,"title":"","content":"This may come as a shock to some people, but we are not consciously aware of everything our own brains do. In fact, the vast majority of our mental processes are unconscious. As a person who lives in the real world, your imagination is inspired by the real world, whether you realize it or not. There is no other source from which to be inspired, except for the works of other creatives, who were in turn inspired by the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T05:35:12-07:00","id":1336534,"title":"","content":"Well said, Willow.<br /> <br /> And yes, drugs count as \u201cthe real world,\u201d before someone cracks <i>that</i> joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T05:43:14-07:00","id":1336535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336510#post1336510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They come from the depths of my vore fetish, which was developed after finding Beachfox's artwork. Not because a tribe of people in the real world partook of human flesh at some point in history.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purposes of what I'm saying, where you get them from doesn't really matter. The point is, they come from your real world experiences, which are shaped by your perceptions, which therefore tells us something about who you are as a person. Like the saying goes, every painting is a self-portrait.<br /> <br /> That's not to say you're necessarily racist for your views on orcs, mind; or at least, no more racist than anyone who's been raised in this racist-ass culture is. HeavyArms already covered the racial implications of using this framework to delineate who's okay to hurt. I'm only saying if you insist your orcs are just orcs and nothing else, I think that's being pretty unfair, because it seems to assume you think you're too special to have been affected by the culture in which you have lived your entire life.<br /> <br /> We all get saddled with baggage along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T06:42:38-07:00","id":1336542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336480#post1336480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any parallels it might have to real life culture is purely coincidental, and not the intentional comparison that others perceive it to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do note that it\u2019s possible to get less-than-coincidental totally by accident, which if anything is where at least half the danger lies in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T07:04:55-07:00","id":1336547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336542#post1336542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do note that it\u2019s possible to get less-than-coincidental totally by accident, which if anything is where at least half the danger lies in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course, but I will not apologize for a crime I didn't commit. If there are allegorical similarities between fantasy and reality when I did not intend for them to be there, then that's just an unfortunate coincidence.<br /> <br /> As I said, I'm not very worldly educated about the various cultures and ethnic groups of real life. That unfortunate fact is one of the major reasons why I find it difficult to get into Scion as much as I would have otherwise liked. The only pantheon I feel like I could accurately portray would be the Theoi, and that's only because I was a huge fan of Greek mythology when I was growing up. As for Greek culture itself, about the only thing I know is togas, democracy, and fans of philosophy.<br /> <br /> Even if I was actively trying to portray someone in an allegorical format, I wouldn't know enough about them to make it past a very basic rough draft, hashed together from whatever pop culture references I could grab off wikipedia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2019, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T07:45:42-07:00","id":1336554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336330#post1336330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay I am reading some hostility in this response, and maybe I'm wrong because this is typing and tone doesn't always have 100% Clarity. I never said this is something people shouldn't do or its wrong, I said I would prefer not to do this because I only play table top games with my personal friends. Contracts are made to protect certain parties in an agreement, ideally all parties but these type of things are made bare minimum to cover the GM's ass. It rather than just watch out for my own bum I want my players to know they can talk with me about issues with the game or even change or clarify things, rather than have that extra step of a physical contract.<br /> <br /> Writing game notes is for characters and setting and not for the players. Having a physical contract you have everyone sign to play a game comes off as cold and sterile. I prefer to talk with my players and develop a rapport. When you just have someone check mark and sign a preprinted document there is a lot of room for people overlook things, and I know a lot people who find even one page character sheets too much information. Personally I like to have at least those two page sheets if not the four page ones. But you should talk with your players and find out what is okay, and what are some expectations for the game. If you have people fill out a form it does not have the same personal touch and things can be overlooked or unclear. I even said it could be a useful tool for con games.<br /> <br /> But for some people, I would argue a lot of people, they would find it uncomfortable to put on paper a list of deepest soul deep fears, especially when you can just talk privately to your game master. Its not really fun to have someone be able to look at a glance and know vulnerable aspects of who you are, concerning things like assault and other traumatic experiences, and I don't think people should have to fill out such a form if they don't want to, as a game master you are not entitled to such intimate knowledge when they can just have a private discussion away from the group.<br /> <br /> I pointed out I had an issue with the arbitrary inclusion of Spiders and Rats because that should be represented by the fill in the blank option, otherwise why don't you have Centipedes and Snakes? Centipedes and Snakes are just as likely to be a fear as Spiders and Rats, and I would argue more people are afraid of Centipedes then they are of Spiders. Everyone I know who is afraid of spiders also fears centipedes, meanwhile I know people who won't bat an eye at a spider but do not want to have anything to do with centipedes. What about Dogs? I love dogs personally, but people who are afraid of dogs usually have it rooted in a traumatic childhood memory. My point is it is arbitrary to just have Spiders and Rats on the sheet, its not so common that it needs to be on there because if it needs to be on there then other things need to be on there as well. I never said there was nobody who can't deal with Arachnid imagery, I'm saying that is what the fill in the blank space is for.<br /> <br /> Just talk with your players, its common sense if you are playing with a friend and she lost her eye to a dog mauling that you shouldn't rub that in their face. Lists aren't comprehensive so it is better to have them just tell you rather than play 20 Questions. This has been in the books for a long time, books from your company, they say talk to your players. This sheet can be a useful tool but it doesn't replace actually communication.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I have no hostility towards you, nor did I write the post angrily or to attack you. Sorry if it came off that way.<br /> <br /> Where in the book did you read that the checklist is a contract of any sort, because I did not get that impression and might have missed it?<br /> <br /> In terms of what is on the checklist, the examples listed besides the blanks are just examples and yes, to that extent, they are arbitrary. Maybe Shanna and Sean polled their friends, I have no idea how they arrived at what was put on there. My point to you is: so what? Those things have no bearing on the overall usefulness of the checklist to perform as intended.<br /> <br /> When I said, from what you're saying you won't be using it as written, that wasn't a condemnation, it was to point out that using it is not mandated by anybody and if you and your group are cool with talking things through, then that's all that matters for you. The point of the book and the checklist is that even among folks who have gamed for a while, there are gaps in that communication that something like the checklist could help fill in. Nevermind trying to get clear lines of what makes folks not enjoy a game when complete strangers sit down at a store or convention. Trying to make those people feel more comfortable and involved with our hobby is what the book is about, and if it can do that, then that's a good thing, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T08:06:58-07:00","id":1336558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336542#post1336542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do note that it\u2019s possible to get less-than-coincidental totally by accident, which if anything is where at least half the danger lies in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, it doesn\u2019t really matter if it\u2019s coincidental or not. What matters is the effects of our actions, not the intent behind them. If I drive my car into a space that is coincidentally occupied by another car, I\u2019m responsible for the damages, regardless of if it was my intent to cause them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T08:10:53-07:00","id":1336560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336547#post1336547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, but I will not apologize for a crime I didn't commit. If there are allegorical similarities between fantasy and reality when I did not intend for them to be there, then that's just an unfortunate coincidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should mention crime, because in the law, intent doesn\u2019t matter for much. Sure, manslaughter isn\u2019t punished as severely as murder, but it\u2019s still a crime. Just because it\u2019s not your intent to do harm doesn\u2019t mean your actions can't be harmful, or that you aren\u2019t still responsible for the harm they cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T08:12:08-07:00","id":1336561,"title":"","content":"So on the original subject of this thread (which lasted more or less for one page before it devolved into &quot;racism and etc.&quot; thread, more or less), I think that my main issue with it is the checklist. I mean, I do recognize that every person has things they would not like to feature in a game, but playing an RPG is a social gathering. Having each person signing a contract of what cause them feel bad during a game and what doesn't feels, well, forced. It feels like going out with friends, but beforehand we all sign a paper where we proclaim on which subjects we should avoid talking, but it cause us feel uncomfortable (or outright getting a panic attack).<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that the players and the GM should not talk about what they would or would not like in their game. On the contrary- they should <i>talk</i> about it. If there is something you would really, really don't want to have in a game, you should talk about it with the other players. If something which goes beyond what you would like to have in a game happens, you should talk with your GM about it. And after a very, difficult scene, the players should all sit together with each other and talk about whether or not one of the players or the GM have crosses the lines. It happened in the group I play in where one of the players turned the corpse of the fallen villain into a sock puppet. It was way too much for me, as well as for some players, and so we talked about it. Also when one of the players have killed some NPC without the consent of the rest of the group. Again, we talked about it- and while we have not reached a consensus, we did reached a concord. <br /> <br /> In short, I don't think that having a checklist about &quot;what subjects bother me and what doesn't&quot; because it feel like it replaces a real, human interaction where players talk about subjects which bothers them. More than that, some players may discover that subjects that they did not mentioned in the checklist actually bothers them, while those they thought did were actually a way to deal with issues they couldn't have in real life. And it is also really hard to bother to predict what would cause a certain player to feel uncomfortable. For example, one of my players took it really hard that I gave them a writing exercise in order to develop their characters, saying that I forced her to write against her will. I explained to her that I had no idea that she took it that hard, as she never said anything, and that next time if I tell her to do something she doesn't like, that she would please inform me about it. <br /> <br /> I mean, when asking a player to expand the backstory of their character could cause a player discomfort, I can't really see the use for such a checklist. Talk with your group, don't force them to fill a piece of paper. That's my opinion, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T08:18:18-07:00","id":1336562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336560#post1336560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny you should mention crime, because in the law, intent doesn\u2019t matter for much. Sure, manslaughter isn\u2019t punished as severely as murder, but it\u2019s still a crime. Just because it\u2019s not your intent to do harm doesn\u2019t mean your actions can't be harmful, or that you aren\u2019t still responsible for the harm they cause.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps, but there is a pretty substantial difference between accidentally ending somebody's life, and accidentally misrepresenting somebody you weren't even trying to imitate in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T08:28:36-07:00","id":1336564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, but I will not apologize for a crime I didn't commit. If there are allegorical similarities between fantasy and reality when I did not intend for them to be there, then that's just an unfortunate coincidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Of course, but I will not apologize for stepping on your foot. If I stepped on your foot when I did not intend to, then that's an unfortunate coincidence.&quot;*<br /> <br /> Of course, I assume in this scenario a person who stepped on another person's foot would at least be therefore mindful of not stepping on other people's feet afterwards, as opposed to obstinately continuing to just tread where they will, other people's feet be damned.<br /> <br /> Like, no one is asking people who make these mistakes to get nailed to a cross they carried up the hill, we just want people to learn from the mistake and move on. It's not a big deal. Is it such a big deal to just be accountable?<br /> <br /> *Alternatively, &quot;Of course, but I will not apologize for crashing into your car and maiming you. If I crashed a car and maimed you when I did not intend to, then that's an unfortunate coincidence.&quot; I have a million of these, and none of them sound good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T08:32:37-07:00","id":1336565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336564#post1336564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Of course, but I will not apologize for stepping on your foot. If I stepped on your foot when I did not intend to, then that's an unfortunate coincidence.&quot;*<br /> <br /> Of course, I assume in this scenario a person who stepped on another person's foot would at least be therefore mindful of not stepping on other people's feet afterwards, as opposed to obstinately continuing to just tread where they will, other people's feet be damned.<br /> <br /> Like, no one is asking people who make these mistakes to get nailed to a cross they carried up the hill, we just want people to learn from the mistake and move on. It's not a big deal. Is it such a big deal to just be accountable?<br /> <br /> *Alternatively, &quot;Of course, but I will not apologize for crashing into your car and maiming you. If I crashed a car and maimed you when I did not intend to, then that's an unfortunate coincidence.&quot; I have a million of these, and none of them sound good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please see my above post, if you want me to reply to that laughable attempt at countering my argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T09:01:32-07:00","id":1336570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336562#post1336562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, but there is a pretty substantial difference between accidentally ending somebody's life, and accidentally misrepresenting somebody you weren't even trying to imitate in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course there is. I don\u2019t think anyone would dispute that. Unintentionally including some unfortunate implications in one\u2019s creative work is not some heinous act deserving of serious punishment. Indeed, it\u2019s something pretty much all creators do from time to time. The issue is not that you accidentally included racist undertones in your writing or your game or whatever, the issue is that when the presence of these undertones is pointed out, instead of taking the critique seriously, apologizing for any harm you may have unintentionally caused, and striving to be more aware of the potential impact of one\u2019s creative work in the future, you attempt to dodge responsibility and make excuses, or worse claim that no harm was actually done.<br /> <br /> Arc may have been a little hyperbolic with the car accident thing, but the analogy to stepping on someone\u2019s foot is a very apt one. If you stepped on someone\u2019s foot by accident, would you claim that you shouldn\u2019t have to apologize for a crime you didn\u2019t commit, or try to argue that there is no problem? I don\u2019t imagine so. I\u2019d like to think you would say, \u201coh, sorry, I didn\u2019t mean to step on your foot,\u201d and probably try not to do it again. So why is your response to having it pointed out that your fantasy setting has some pretty uncomfortable themes surrounding race any different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T09:35:32-07:00","id":1336576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336547#post1336547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, but I will not apologize for a crime I didn't commit.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is the part that\u2019s rubbing people the wrong way and for good reason. People apologize all the time for things they did by accident, it\u2019s a very normal and considerate thing to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336558#post1336558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, it doesn\u2019t really matter if it\u2019s coincidental or not. What matters is the effects of our actions, not the intent behind them. If I drive my car into a space that is coincidentally occupied by another car, I\u2019m responsible for the damages, regardless of if it was my intent to cause them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s exactly what I was pointing out, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T09:39:45-07:00","id":1336578,"title":"","content":"The hyperbole is more there to point down the way of myriad examples. The idea at work sucks in any of it's incarnations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T10:18:26-07:00","id":1336588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336570#post1336570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course there is. I don\u2019t think anyone would dispute that. Unintentionally including some unfortunate implications in one\u2019s creative work is not some heinous act deserving of serious punishment. Indeed, it\u2019s something pretty much all creators do from time to time. The issue is not that you accidentally included racist undertones in your writing or your game or whatever, the issue is that when the presence of these undertones is pointed out, instead of taking the critique seriously, apologizing for any harm you may have unintentionally caused, and striving to be more aware of the potential impact of one\u2019s creative work in the future, you attempt to dodge responsibility and make excuses, or worse claim that no harm was actually done.<br /> <br /> Arc may have been a little hyperbolic with the car accident thing, but the analogy to stepping on someone\u2019s foot is a very apt one. If you stepped on someone\u2019s foot by accident, would you claim that you shouldn\u2019t have to apologize for a crime you didn\u2019t commit, or try to argue that there is no problem? I don\u2019t imagine so. I\u2019d like to think you would say, \u201coh, sorry, I didn\u2019t mean to step on your foot,\u201d and probably try not to do it again. So why is your response to having it pointed out that your fantasy setting has some pretty uncomfortable themes surrounding race any different?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, according to what others have previously stated on this thread, a person's imagination is influenced by memories and real world experiences. And if that's the kind of thought process we're going by, then to me it sounds like it would be nigh impossible to include any degree of world building in a setting, because the cultures we design &quot;have to come from somewhere&quot; and chances are, that somewhere is derived from people who exist in real life. It sounds like I'm going to offend somebody no matter what I do, so my only option is to simply accept the fact that I can't please everyone, or else give up trying to create any kind of story at all.<br /> <br /> If I might back track a little on my last cannibal comment. I would like to try and clarify that I enjoy the <b>concept</b> of there being characters in the setting who engage in that sort of stuff. I enjoy the <b>idea</b> of a quiet little town that secretly engages in demon worship. I enjoy the <b>fantasy</b> of there being a tribe of huge, burly warriors that go on raids and pillage the countryside. I enjoy the <b>trope</b> of Goblins being crazy little anarchists.<br /> <br /> That is all these characters are to me, ideas, tropes and fantasies that I choose to include within the narrative because I enjoy their concepts. They are not meant to be an actual correlation to any existing peoples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T10:22:20-07:00","id":1336591,"title":"","content":"In general if I hurt someone and didn't mean to do it, I'll apologize for doing it. While I didn't intend to do harm to that person, I did harm them nevertheless and they deserve an apology for that. On the other hand if I hurt someone because I <i>intended</i> to hurt them, then I'm not going to apologize for hurting them (or if I do apologize it would probably be a very sarcastic and demeaning one). <br /> <br /> So in my experience, if Person A hurts Person B, and Person B points this out (&quot;Hey, that hurt. Please don't do that.&quot;) and Person A refuses to issue an apology or stop doing it, my first thought is going to be that either Person A <i>intended</i> to hurt Person B to begin with, or simply does not care at all that he hurt Person B, which makes Person A, at the absolute best, a jerk.<br /> <br /> Note that I'm not calling anyone in this thread a jerk, but this is my general &quot;default&quot; thought process when I see someone get hurt in some way, even by accident, and there's a refusal to issue any sort of apology for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T10:26:05-07:00","id":1336594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336588#post1336588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, according to what others have previously stated on this thread, a person's imagination is influenced by memories and real world experiences. And if that's the kind of thought process we're going by, then to me it sounds like it would be nigh impossible to include any degree of world building in a setting, because the cultures we design &amp;quot;have to come from somewhere&amp;quot; and chances are, that somewhere is derived from people who exist in real life. It sounds like I'm going to offend somebody no matter what I do, so my only option is to simply accept the fact that I can't please everyone, or else give up trying to create any kind of story at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, maybe not, and the way to find out for any given player/group is to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T10:31:26-07:00","id":1336596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like I'm going to offend somebody no matter what I do, so my only option is to simply accept the fact that I can't please everyone, or else give up trying to create any kind of story at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I can't be bothered to stop hurting you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Truly the superior argument!<br /> <br /> Dude, I'm telling you as someone who was making your arguments back in 2010-<i>it's not that big of a deal to just try</i>. You learn, you practice, you get good at it, and you keep at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T10:40:56-07:00","id":1336597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336591#post1336591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general if I hurt someone and didn't mean to do it, I'll apologize for doing it. While I didn't intend to do harm to that person, I did harm them nevertheless and they deserve an apology for that. On the other hand if I hurt someone because I <i>intended</i> to hurt them, then I'm not going to apologize for hurting them (or if I do apologize it would probably be a very sarcastic and demeaning one).<br /> <br /> So in my experience, if Person A hurts Person B, and Person B points this out (&quot;Hey, that hurt. Please don't do that.&quot;) and Person A refuses to issue an apology or stop doing it, my first thought is going to be that either Person A <i>intended</i> to hurt Person B to begin with, or simply does not care at all that he hurt Person B, which makes Person A, at the absolute best, a jerk.<br /> <br /> Note that I'm not calling anyone in this thread a jerk, but this is my general &quot;default&quot; thought process when I see someone get hurt in some way, even by accident, and there's a refusal to issue any sort of apology for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay, so then answer me this: Who should I apologize to? If I include a tribe of generic cannibals in the story, should I offer an official declaration to every culture in the world who ever had a period of eating humans at some point in their history?<br /> <br /> If I include a generic band of marauding soldiers / barbarians / mercenaries, should I apologize to... oh... how about 100% of the global population? Because I'm pretty sure our ancestors did not exactly get along with each other throughout most of history.<br /> <br /> If you truly want an apology from me in order to feel better about the situation, then fine, I apologize that my generic fantasy trope offended you in some way. But that doesn't mean I'm going to scrap the entire setting and rebuild it from scratch in the vain hope of creating a mature themed story that everybody in the world can enjoy together.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13313_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13313\" data-vbnamecard=\"13313\">Sith_Happens</a><br /> <br /> Yes, that should be addressed preferably before the session begins, rather than partway through. Preferably without giving away plot spoilers, if you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2019, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T11:08:42-07:00","id":1336600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336597#post1336597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so then answer me this: Who should I apologize to? If I include a tribe of generic cannibals in the story, should I offer an official declaration to every culture in the world who ever had a period of eating humans at some point in their history?<br /> <br /> If I include a generic band of marauding soldiers / barbarians / mercenaries, should I apologize to... oh... how about 100% of the global population? Because I'm pretty sure our ancestors did not exactly get along with each other throughout most of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it doesn't seem hard to me.<br /> <br /> If one of your players says, &quot;Hey, were you aware that this group of X that you designed contains a lot of tropes or ideas that are problematic and have been used as a way to oppress or hurt people. I didn't care much for that,&quot; I think the proper response would be to go, &quot;Whoops. I didn't mean to do that and wasn't aware of it. Sorry if you or anyone else found that offensive or upsetting!&quot; That's really all it takes.<br /> <br /> If you want, you can then go on, &quot;Here was my thought process for how I created this group of people and why I designed them to embody elements that I was not aware were offensive or would upset anyone. Since I obviously don't want to upset the people playing in my game session, and don't want them coming away from my game thinking I'm a jerk or anything, do you have any idea on how this group could be modified to be less offensive without losing the the themes and ideas that I feel they need to embody?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ultimately RPGs are a collaborative experience, so if your players aren't enjoying it because they find certain elements to be problematic, and tell you why they're not enjoying it, then it would be in your best interest to work with them to make things more enjoyable for them. Because if they're enjoying your game, you'll enjoy running your game. If they don't like it, you won't have much fun running it either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T11:10:08-07:00","id":1336601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336597#post1336597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so then answer me this: Who should I apologize to? If I include a tribe of generic cannibals in the story, should I offer an official declaration to every culture in the world who ever had a period of eating humans at some point in their history?<br /> <br /> If I include a generic band of marauding soldiers / barbarians / mercenaries, should I apologize to... oh... how about 100% of the global population? Because I'm pretty sure our ancestors did not exactly get along with each other throughout most of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should apologize to the people negativity impacted by your actions. I\u2019m sure as hell not affected by you including a race of cannibals or a race of warlike marauders in your story. But if someone tells you they are hurt by it, that\u2019d be the person to apologize to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336597#post1336597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you truly want an apology from me in order to feel better about the situation, then fine, I apologize that my generic fantasy trope offended you in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a non-apology. This is the equivalent of, when you step on someone\u2019s foot, saying \u201csorry your foot got hurt\u201d instead of \u201csorry I hurt your foot.\u201d It\u2019s still an attempt to absolve yourself of responsibility for what happened, when the whole point of an apology is to show that you are accepting responsibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336597#post1336597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that doesn't mean I'm going to scrap the entire setting and rebuild it from scratch in the vain hope of creating a mature themed story that everybody in the world can enjoy together.</div> </div> </div> </div>This whole side-tangent started because Heavy Arms, a member of a historically (and currently) oppressed group of people pointed out that calling your universally evil creatures a \u201crace\u201d opens the door for comparison to real-life groups of humans. In this situation, I think the responsible thing to do would not be to remove all groups of evil creatures in your story, but to <i>stop calling those groups of creatures \u201craces.\u201d</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T11:11:32-07:00","id":1336603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336600#post1336600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it doesn't seem hard to me.<br /> <br /> If one of your players says, &amp;quot;Hey, were you aware that this group of X that you designed contains a lot of tropes or ideas that are problematic and have been used as a way to oppress or hurt people. I didn't care much for that,&amp;quot; I think the proper response would be to go, &amp;quot;Whoops. I didn't mean to do that and wasn't aware of it. Sorry if you or anyone else found that offensive or upsetting!&amp;quot; That's really all it takes.<br /> <br /> If you want, you can then go on, &amp;quot;Here was my thought process for how I created this group of people and why I designed them to embody elements that I was not aware were offensive or would upset anyone. Since I obviously don't want to upset the people playing in my game session, and don't want them coming away from my game thinking I'm a jerk or anything, do you have any idea on how this group could be modified to be less offensive without losing the the themes and ideas that I feel they need to embody?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Ultimately RPGs are a collaborative experience, so if your players aren't enjoying it because they find certain elements to be problematic, and tell you why they're not enjoying it, then it would be in your best interest to work with them to make things more enjoyable for them. Because if they're enjoying your game, you'll enjoy running your game. If they don't like it, you won't have much fun running it either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T11:37:02-07:00","id":1336608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336601#post1336601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should apologize to the people negativity impacted by your actions. I\u2019m sure as hell not affected by you including a race of cannibals or a race of warlike marauders in your story. But if someone tells you they are hurt by it, that\u2019d be the person to apologize to.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a non-apology. This is the equivalent of, when you step on someone\u2019s foot, saying \u201csorry your foot got hurt\u201d instead of \u201csorry I hurt your foot.\u201d It\u2019s still an attempt to absolve yourself of responsibility for what happened, when the whole point of an apology is to show that you are accepting responsibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I'm not accepting responsibility. A generic trope is just that, generic. It doesn't relate to anything specific beyond a simplified concept, which the creator is then free to expand upon however they wish. And as for being negatively impacted, I would politely ask for clarification as to how the story harmed them in any manner beyond hurting their feelings.<br /> <br /> Now, if people looked at my story and decided that the appropriate response was to organize a lynch mob and hunt down a specific group of people, then yes, I would publicly denounce such responses and call those who partook in it a bunch of morons. But if the worst thing to happen is that somebody chose to read too deeply into the material and put themselves through a series of mental gymnastics to arrive at the conclusion that it was some kind of personal attack, then the only thing I can derive from that is that said person is either self absorbed, or very insecure about themselves.<br /> <br /> As I said before, I can not control what people choose to take away from my work. And as long as the overall narrative is intended for a mature audience, it is going to include dark, adult themes. Themes which many people may not be comfortable with. And that's fine, I'm not going to demean and belittle them because they can't handle certain content. But this is the kind of content that I built the narrative around, and if it upsets them, then we should either discuss it before the game begins, so that we can make some adjustments if need be (fade to black is always a good option), or we can politely suggest that they go look for another game to join so that I don't have to hold up the rest of the group by retconning things in the middle of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2019, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T11:41:30-07:00","id":1336609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336561#post1336561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having each person signing a contract of what cause them feel bad during a game and what doesn't feels, well, forced.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a contract... it's a questionnaire. You don't sign it, it's not meant to be immutable or legally binding. Another important thing? Green. It's also about what you want to see in the game, not just what you don't want to see in the game.<br /> <br /> And it might feel forced... but to an extent that's necessary. Lots of people have issues with their consent being violated in RPGs (just in terms of things like content and so on), the process of adding consent tools to work to reduce this is inherently artificial. <br /> <br /> Consider it something like speed limits, but without legal enforcement.<br /> <br /> For a long time, we didn't bother with speed limits (mostly because people couldn't go fast enough for it to matter). But we noticed a correlation between high speed and dangerous accidents. So we put up speed limits to say, &quot;hey this road isn't very safe for going so fast.&quot; Even though in reality, speed limits are pretty conservative and an experienced and responsible driver could go in excess of them safely, it's better to encourage people to slow down rather than trust everyone is at that level of skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In short, I don't think that having a checklist about &quot;what subjects bother me and what doesn't&quot; because it feel like it replaces a real, human interaction where players talk about subjects which bothers them.<br /> ...<br /> Talk with your group, don't force them to fill a piece of paper. </div> </div> </div>Sorry for chopping this up, but I want to address the broader point first and some specifics second.<br /> <br /> The whole problem with this is asserting that writing things down, or using a form, isn't communication. It is. It might not be the totality of the conversation (the form directly has a section to remind you of that), but it's still communication.<br /> <br /> <b>Not everyone is actually comfortable having open frank conversations about deeply person issues</b>.<br /> <br /> Maybe this is because you're at a convention and this is a bunch of strangers and you don't want to talk about your phobia in detail.<br /> <br /> Maybe you're feeling socially awkward and unassertive and having the whole group there shuts you down and you don't speak up.<br /> <br /> Maybe you're feeling the social pressure to go with the flow and while everyone else is talking about how awesome X is, X is actually something you can't stand but you don't want to be the one to poo poo on the fun... so you don't say anything.<br /> <br /> Maybe, even if friends you've known for years, you have things you've never told them because they're traumatic and we've been conditioned by society to feel shame about them so we stuff them away instead of telling people.<br /> <br /> There are countless variations that come to the same point: &quot;talk with your group,&quot; doesn't work, because it's not enough. Maybe the checklist isn't the right thing for your situation, but some other extra tool probably is. The ideal world were we can all just sit down and talk, trusting the situation to be safe for open conversations about any topic is a fantasy. A good fantasy we should strive to get to as close to as we can, but not reality. Reality is that we sit down to talk as a group, thinking - like economists assuming people are always sane and rational actors - everyone's going to say everything that needs to be said, and that the job is done, but lots didn't get said for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> One method of communication doesn't work. If you really want to maximize people's openness to speak up? You need to give them options for engaging so they find one that's comfortable for them, even if it's not convenient or easy for everyone to put in that effort. Consent tools are just more methods of communication. A form is real human interaction. An X-card is talking with your group. Maybe, again, not the whole conversation, but dismissing these things as somehow &quot;fake&quot; communication is not healthy for increasing consent based practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More than that, some players may discover that subjects that they did not mentioned in the checklist actually bothers them, while those they thought did were actually a way to deal with issues they couldn't have in real life. </div> </div> </div>If consent cannot be given or revoked after the beginning of the activity, then there's no safe way to assume consent at all. The form is a starting point... just like sitting down and talking to people before the game starts is. It's not mean to be set in stone and unchangeable as things progress, any more than telling your group that you don't like clowns means you can't say, &quot;Hey, I know clowns are really not my thing, but even I think it would be neat to put a clown in this, so yeah, lets have a clown in this scene and see how it goes.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, one of my players took it really hard that I gave them a writing exercise in order to develop their characters, saying that I forced her to write against her will. </div> </div> </div>Was, &quot;the GM is allow to assign you writing homework,&quot; part of something you discussed as a group? Or just something you assumed is normal?<br /> <br /> I mean, this is kind of a consent 101 example here. With the power dynamics of GM to player, unless something like this is something you've made sure is explicit and clearly understood to be a power of the GM to do, you don't assign out-of-play work to people. It's not your job to force writing assignments on your players unless they actively agree to make it your job.<br /> <br /> It's extremely different to ask a player if they're interesting in a writing project for this purpose, than to actually assign it to them.<br /> <br /> I really don't think you've considered how creepy this story sounds. I'm going to put this in a different context for the purposes of illustration:<br /> <br /> &quot;It's really hard to predict what women will get uncomfortable about. For example, one time I assigned my wife dish-washing duties to help her expand how she contributes to the household chores. She took it really hard and said I was forcing her to wash dishes against her will. I explained to her that I had no idea that she'd take it so hard, as she'd never said anything, and that text time if I tell her to do something she doesn't like, that she would please inform me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does that.... sound like a GM that got caught of guard, or someone you'd call the cops on to report domestic abuse? Maybe it's fine. I know people where that's a negotiated part of the relationship (24/7 TPE is a thing, and more power to them if they consent to it). But it still sounds really messed up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I explained to her that I had no idea that she took it that hard, as she never said anything, and that next time if I tell her to do something she doesn't like, that she would please inform me about it. </div> </div> </div>Not getting &quot;no&quot; is not the same as getting &quot;yes.&quot; If she never said yes especially, assuming her not saying something was a yes is why we need consent education and tool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336588#post1336588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not meant to be an actual correlation to any existing peoples.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ultimately not your decision to make.<br /> <br /> You don't get to retroactively eliminate all the negative associations something has just because you want to use it for a perfectly fine reason that has nothing to do with those associations. They exist, and they upset people, and no amount of what you mean will change that. You can't use the Confederate flag and say you don't want people to think about slavery and racism. It doesn't work that way. It doesn't matter that it's a neat design and you just want it because of that.<br /> <br /> Other people created the correlations before you got there. Ignoring it solves nothing. It's not actually the end of all possibilities, it just means making it work takes more effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T11:49:40-07:00","id":1336611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336597#post1336597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who should I apologize to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Me for the whole dwarf mess wouldn't be a bad one if you sincerely meant it. Specifically the whole victim-blaming rant about how me pointing out the bigoted tropes Tolkien used made it somehow my fault that apparently you view the world in a more bigoted light just by knowing what bigots did to my people so you can avoid doing the same thing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T12:01:33-07:00","id":1336618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336561#post1336561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, when asking a player to expand the backstory of their character could cause a player discomfort, I can't really see the use for such a checklist. Talk with your group, don't force them to fill a piece of paper. That's my opinion, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree. At the same time though, there are definitely situations where a piece of paper like this could be useful.<br /> <br /> First, some players might feel a little uncomfortable in talking with someone they don't know all that well, especially if they're worried about the ST or other players deciding to play &quot;armchair psychologist,&quot; whereas they might be more willing to be upfront if it's just a matter of filling in a piece of paper. The paper creates a certain level of detachment which can be useful for players who might have trouble talking about stuff that they have problem with. It can give them &quot;a place to start.&quot;<br /> <br /> A paper like this could also be really useful when dealing with players who are new to the table or even RPGs entirely. These players might not realize they need to (or even can!) mention to the ST which elements that could appear in a game would be problematic for them. At the very least, a paper like this wouldn't be a bad way to kickstart the conversation and get players more aware of the fact that they can give input on what sort of things they would prefer not to see in a game.<br /> <br /> Of course, like was mentioned, it's not a contract or anything and doesn't mean an ST <i>can't</i> include those elements. But if the ST does feel that it's necessary for to use those elements in his game, he will at least know that he needs to do so gingerly or more carefully to avoid harming the fun of the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T12:36:42-07:00","id":1336621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336611#post1336611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Me for the whole dwarf mess wouldn't be a bad one if you sincerely meant it. Specifically the whole victim-blaming rant about how me pointing out the bigoted tropes Tolkien used made it somehow my fault that apparently you view the world in a more bigoted light just by knowing what bigots did to my people so you can avoid doing the same thing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, my argument was never insinuating that Jews were responsible for the whole dwarf mess. What I was trying to get across to you is how ridiculous it was to draw attention to the fact that the negative aspects of dwarves should be stereotypes associated with your people. And for people like me, who didn't even recognize those were stereotypes, much less who they related to, your behavior seemed extremely counter productive to what you were trying to achieve.<br /> <br /> If you want people to stop viewing you in terms of negative stereotypes, then you allow those stereotypes to fade into obscurity. The news that somebody like me never even considered the idea that your people were greedy alcoholics should have been a cause for celebration, not outrage. But yet, you seem to be of the mindset that it's a good thing to keep these negative viewpoints fresh in people's minds, rather than allowing them to move beyond it. I mean for god sakes, you actually went out of your way to explain to me in detail why the public thinks Jews might have a drinking problem.<br /> <br /> And what does that get you? Nothing, beyond extending your people's suffering, by conditioning future generations to view them in the same manner that their ass hole parents did.<br /> <br /> What exactly are you asking me to apologize for? <i><b>I'm sorry for not being antisemitic?</b></i> Because that sure sounds like what you want me to say!<br /> <br /> Don't think that I am completely without sympathy. I too have been marginalized by bigoted hate groups throughout my life. Both in terms of my sexuality, as well as my mental capacity. I've suffered verbal, physical, emotional and even sexual abuse, just like several other people on these forums. I know how painful and infuriating that kind of bullshit can be, and I am intimately aware of how persistent the emotional scars can be. And I do not want to constantly revisit that pain, by drawing attention to it every time somebody does something remotely similar to what I had to suffer through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2019, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T13:18:42-07:00","id":1336638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336608#post1336608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I'm not accepting responsibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? \u201cWhoops, my bad, that\u2019s not what I going for at all\u201d is not a hard thing to say. If anything it makes them much more receptive to you then explaining what you <i>were</i> going for and asking if they think they\u2019re capable of thinking of it that way, which is clearly your preferred approach.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you really have to think of it as a white lie then go ahead, from a practical perspective the important part is that saying it is only going to help the situation even or especially if you follow up with \u201cHere\u2019s why I think we can make this work.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 09-18-2019, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T13:27:43-07:00","id":1336640,"title":"","content":"When people aren\u2019t aware of the ways certain groups are marginalized and oppressed, those oppressions can more easily fly under the radar. Better to take the \u201cwell I didn\u2019t know that was a racist stereotype\u201d excuse away from people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T13:37:50-07:00","id":1336644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336638#post1336638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not? \u201cWhoops, my bad, that\u2019s not what I going for at all\u201d is not a hard thing to say. If anything it makes them much more receptive to you then explaining what you <i>were</i> going for and asking if they think they\u2019re capable of thinking of it that way, which is clearly your preferred approach.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did say that I wasn't going for that at all. Multiple times, and ad nauseam. Yet, they refused to accept that response and insisted up and down that my intentions didn't matter, as long as the damage was done. At this point, I have no idea what else I can say to convince them that I was not trying to be disrespectful, or aggressive towards anybody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2019, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T14:03:29-07:00","id":1336653,"title":"","content":"Was talking about a hypothetical game, not this thread. It\u2019s obviously too late to try the tactic in question here in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T14:17:01-07:00","id":1336658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336621#post1336621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I was trying to get across to you is how ridiculous it was to draw attention to the fact that the negative aspects of dwarves should be stereotypes associated with your people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, you're blaming me (the victim of systemic long historied bigotry) for drawing your attention to stuff that bigots did. I didn't want fantasy dwarves coded as Jews. I didn't ask Tolkien to do that. He did that far before I was born. I don't want people to repeat his bigotry mindlessly. Your response is still to blame me for being the problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want people to stop viewing you in terms of negative stereotypes, then you allow those stereotypes to fade into obscurity. </div> </div> </div>Ignoring Nazis has never made Nazis go away.<br /> <br /> Teaching people who believe Nazis are bad, what things Nazis use as code to disguise their bigotry helps people that think Nazis are bad to know what to look for to spot Nazis and help stop them.<br /> <br /> You can't ignore negative stereotypes out of existence, because they are bad people actively keeping them going. So you have to inform all the people that aren't bad people what the bad people are doing, so they don't accidentally help the bad people.<br /> <br /> Why is this so fucking hard to grasp?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yet, you seem to be of the mindset that it's a good thing to keep these negative viewpoints fresh in people's minds, rather than allowing them to move beyond it. </div> </div> </div><b>People kill Jews because of those stereotypes</b>. Not killed in the past, not something long gone to history. It's still happening. I can't &quot;move beyond,&quot; people wanting to kill me because of bigoted nonsense. I have to defend myself against that, and that means I need good people to know what's going on to stand with me, not whine about how I'm harshing their buzz and how they'd like to play games while my life is on the line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What exactly are you asking me to apologize for? </div> </div> </div>See above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't think that I am completely without sympathy. </div> </div> </div>Demonstrate some then. Words about your own pain only show a lack of sympathy because you have no interest in helping others avoid it, just protecting yourself from feeling a sliver of it again.<br /> <br /> Right now, if we were magically transported back in time to Nazi Germany, I 100% believe you'd out me as a Jew on the spot to save yourself. That's what you've said over multiple threads makes me think about your &quot;sympathy&quot; and commitment to being a good person to your fellow humans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T14:30:14-07:00","id":1336664,"title":"","content":"I feel like we've reached the point where the conversation has run it's course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T15:51:19-07:00","id":1336692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336588#post1336588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, according to what others have previously stated on this thread, a person's imagination is influenced by memories and real world experiences. And if that's the kind of thought process we're going by, then to me it sounds like it would be nigh impossible to include any degree of world building in a setting, because the cultures we design &quot;have to come from somewhere&quot; and chances are, that somewhere is derived from people who exist in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing a couple of factors here.<br /> <br /> First, not everyone is equally offended by things. Like, there are people who are fine with dwarves being Jewish or orcs being &quot;the least lovely Mongol-types.&quot; If that's the kind of world you want to build (and I know you're not going there, but I'm using an extreme example to demonstrate a principle), then find people who want to play in that world and have fun with it. The only problem comes when you take that out to people who are not the target audience and act like we should like it... well, that and any prods you might feel from your conscience, but that's on you to deal with.<br /> <br /> Second, it is possible to draw inspiration from existing cultures in ways that are respectful, non-appropriative, and not racist. Like, take the movie <b>Black Panther</b> as an example. It draws from several different African cultures, but no one I know of felt it was racist because it was done with a sense of reverence, and an understanding that a culture is not a caricature.<br /> <br /> Third, you're drawing a line at a very self-serving point. You seem to be wanting to be given credit for worldbuilding while ducking responsibility for any problematic implications of your attempts to worldbuild because your orcs don't mean anything, they're just cartoon cannibals. It sounds like you want to have your cake and eat it too, which... well, good luck squaring that circle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T16:20:36-07:00","id":1336695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1335938-consent-in-gaming?p=1336692#post1336692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing a couple of factors here.<br /> <br /> First, not everyone is equally offended by things. Like, there are people who are fine with dwarves being Jewish or orcs being &quot;the least lovely Mongol-types.&quot; If that's the kind of world you want to build (and I know you're not going there, but I'm using an extreme example to demonstrate a principle), then find people who want to play in that world and have fun with it. The only problem comes when you take that out to people who are not the target audience and act like we should like it... well, that and any prods you might feel from your conscience, but that's on you to deal with.<br /> <br /> Second, it is possible to draw inspiration from existing cultures in ways that are respectful, non-appropriative, and not racist. Like, take the movie <b>Black Panther</b> as an example. It draws from several different African cultures, but no one I know of felt it was racist because it was done with a sense of reverence, and an understanding that a culture is not a caricature.<br /> <br /> Third, you're drawing a line at a very self-serving point. You seem to be wanting to be given credit for worldbuilding while ducking responsibility for any problematic implications of your attempts to worldbuild because your orcs don't mean anything, they're just cartoon cannibals. It sounds like you want to have your cake and eat it too, which... well, good luck squaring that circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know that not everybody is okay with the same things. And if that turns out to be the case, I would be perfectly willing to discuss it with the group so that we're all on the same page. To reiterate, the dark, mature themes are simply my default stance on a setting, and not something that I'm insistent on sticking to.<br /> <br /> I never saw the Black Panther movie, but if it was anything like the comic book iteration, then I can only imagine it had at least some scenes which existed purely to hate on white people. As for Wakanda itself, don't let the futuristic,utopian paradise fool you. The Wakandans are ruthlessly jealous about the success of their culture to the point of completely isolating themselves from the rest of the world. Not only that, but they have lined their borders with frankly barbaric defense mechanisms. Like the Panther Jaws, which are giant bear traps that impale you through the chest with sharpened tree branches! And then they just leave the corpses out in the open as a warning to anyone else who tries to cross their borders uninvited.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as I said, I don't know enough about other cultures to try a real take on portraying them in any kind of accurate realism. The similarities would be mostly aesthetic, with some mild inspiration. For example, I think the feudal Japanese architecture looks pretty neat. And if I'm not mistaken, there's an entire nation of Hobgoblins who seem to heavily resemble this kind of society? Hobgoblins dressed in samurai armor reminds me of this:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/8674b800-880e-43c3-9821-175a5844fd48/dbc35zf-750c7100-31df-4c41-a390-b2588be93068.jpg/v1/fill/w_800,h_1252,q_75,strp/oni_by_sceith_a_dbc35zf-fullview.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..umpZO69i78_DR6IHMsb9_TdidmGLJa_VgF4sscqxFyk\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which I think is a pretty cool idea in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T16:49:12-07:00","id":1336706,"title":"","content":"If i turned up to a game and that form got handed out, i would chuckle, then look around. If no one else was laughing, then this group would not be for me. To try and use the vernacular, this would be a hard limit for me. Likewise, i am very cagey about &quot;session 0&quot; stuff. You want to give me an outline of your game for character gen, cool. You start talking about exploring themes, ehhhh. Any mention of lines and veils or traffic lights etc, I'm not going to make it to session one.<br /> <br /> And on the &quot;race&quot; thing, I've never heard an actual person use it to refer to a people. In my experience, even with quite &quot;racist&quot; people, it's not a thing. Except maybe historical sources, like about eugenics or nazi's.<br /> <br /> Of course, on the internet, it's a whole other ballgame, but fortunately, everyone i know in real life is beyond this kind of thing. Hence, a warning flag that I'll not fit in with a group","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24824-notempathic","name":"NotEmpathic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T17:08:14-07:00","id":13